{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling","id":1038176,"title":"Is Mage actually more appropriate for Science Fiction than Changeling?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-25T19:06:01-08:00","id":1038176,"title":"Is Mage actually more appropriate for Science Fiction than Changeling?","content":"In my mind, Science Fiction represents the dreams of the future, so I see Science Fiction as fitting more within the realm of Changeling than Mage (similar to the idea that Fantasy and Horror are actually more fitting for Changeling than Mage). While there are Mage factions that use Hyperscience (or something similar), they really are antithetical to the dreams of Science Fiction and, quite frankly, their members are more likely to be accountants who watch baseball because they enjoy the statistics (or baseball players who take up accounting because they never made the big leagues) than science fiction fans. However, in the Deep Dreaming, you can find any dream, and Science Fiction fills the dreams of hundreds of millions of people (how many people have watched Aliens, Anime, Star Trek, Star Wars, etc), so Changelings could travel the Deep Dreaming to Realms that correspond to Science Fiction series. There, they could join the crew of the U.S.S. Enterprise or fight with the Rebel Alliance against the Empire (or they could hijack the Enterprise or a Star Destroyer in an attempt to bring it back to the real world). What are your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:17:56-08:00","id":1038186,"title":"","content":"Mage has the Sons of Ether, the tradition the literally embodies Sci-Fi.<br /> <br /> Ok, now I've got that out of the way. One of the biggest problems with this is how Changelings cannot survive in banal environments. I know you could argue that &quot;Sci-fi isn't banal!&quot; and I would agree, except that the changeling's definition of banality is not just about imagination, but about accepting whimsy over hard facts and Feel over Think. To a changeling, Star Trek would be horrendously banal, but Star Wars would fair a bit better.<br /> <br /> So I'd say Mage would be better for Scifi stuff, especially an all Etherite game, than a Changeling game which is going to have banality as a lingering factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:28:16-08:00","id":1038194,"title":"","content":"Would it be banal though if the Changelings were exploring the Deep Dreaming? And Star Trek has as little to do with facts as Star Wars, so I doubt that it would be any more banal than Star Wars.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:32:52-08:00","id":1038196,"title":"","content":"It's not about facts. Or truth. It's the attitude. The &quot;We're here to examine things reasonably.&quot; &quot;We're going to use our heads and think things through.&quot; It's less an objective thing than an attitude. You could probably use the trappings of sci fi in changeling with little to no problems. But actually constructing a reasonable sci-fi story?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:35:28-08:00","id":1038201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling#post1038176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my mind, Science Fiction represents the dreams of the future, so I see Science Fiction as fitting more within the realm of Changeling than Mage (similar to the idea that Fantasy and Horror are actually more fitting for Changeling than Mage). While there are Mage factions that use Hyperscience (or something similar), they really are antithetical to the dreams of Science Fiction and, quite frankly, their members are more likely to be accountants who watch baseball because they enjoy the statistics (or baseball players who take up accounting because they never made the big leagues) than science fiction fans. However, in the Deep Dreaming, you can find any dream, and Science Fiction fills the dreams of hundreds of millions of people (how many people have watched Aliens, Anime, Star Trek, Star Wars, etc), so Changelings could travel the Deep Dreaming to Realms that correspond to Science Fiction series. There, they could join the crew of the U.S.S. Enterprise or fight with the Rebel Alliance against the Empire (or they could hijack the Enterprise or a Star Destroyer in an attempt to bring it back to the real world). What are your thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Overly narrow genre conventions are overly narrow pidgeon-holey crap. You can set a game in some futuristic setting and go for either hope or fear. You can set a game in the past and evoke terror or joy. Enjoy the collage: <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://s24.postimg.org/s1fd6j639/Overly_Narrative_11.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:38:59-08:00","id":1038202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038196#post1038196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about facts. Or truth. It's the attitude. The &quot;We're here to examine things reasonably.&quot; &quot;We're going to use our heads and think things through.&quot; It's less an objective thing than an attitude. You could probably use the trappings of sci fi in changeling with little to no problems. But actually constructing a reasonable sci-fi story?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right so changeling works for Every Scifi Movie Hollywood has ever made(especially Promethean and Avatar!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:44:03-08:00","id":1038205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038202#post1038202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Right so changeling works for Every Scifi Movie Hollywood has ever made(especially Promethean and Avatar!)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more a sliding scale from Flash Gordon to 2001: A Space Odyssey","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:44:17-08:00","id":1038206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038202#post1038202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Right so changeling works for Every Scifi Movie Hollywood has ever made(especially Promethean and Avatar!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Yes it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:19:12-08:00","id":1038238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038206#post1038206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, Yes it does.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As long as we admit that maybe only the hardest of hard Scifi might not count for the Dreaming so the vast majority of anything anyone has ever seen that they would think of as scifi works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T09:39:43-08:00","id":1038454,"title":"","content":"If we start admitting things like that, the entire basis for the banality of the modern world starts to crumble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T11:30:11-08:00","id":1038498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my mind, Science Fiction represents the dreams of the future, so I see Science Fiction as fitting more within the realm of Changeling than Mage </div> </div> </div> As someone who hasn't played Changeling, but is aware of the Technocratic Union, can you please elaborate on this thought? Isn't the Union literally made up science to justify magic? Sorry if this is an ignorant thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T11:57:41-08:00","id":1038510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038454#post1038454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we start admitting things like that, the entire basis for the banality of the modern world starts to crumble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily, as Banality is a measure of how poorly you dream and wonder (or fear and have nightmares), and the future that you get isn't necessarily/probably isn't the future that you dreamt of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T12:03:13-08:00","id":1038513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038498#post1038498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As someone who hasn't played Changeling, but is aware of the Technocratic Union, can you please elaborate on this thought? Isn't the Union literally made up science to justify magic? Sorry if this is an ignorant thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Union doesn't dream of the future; in Mage, it has it on a schedule, and in other games, it probably still has some kind of strict regulatory plan in place, to the extent that it can manage in a crossover setting. Step off the schedule or disrupt the plan, and you get removed (killing people will net you temporary Banality, so if you're fine with disappearing people for the sake of a conspiracy, you probably have a lot of it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T13:35:20-08:00","id":1038554,"title":"","content":"The Union seeks to limit and to regulate magic, they are more bureaucrats and accountants than they are scientists. Science is actually something that the Union is not too found of because Science is a hydra (for every question that is answered, two more are spawned). In fact, most magical traditions have been experimental and scientific in their approach throughout history, as magicians and witches have always sought wonder and strived for understanding.<br /> <br /> While people may claim that we have advanced plenty in the last fifty years, the greatest scientific achievement in history was the Apollo Mission. Everything developed since then has been a distraction to prevent the Banality of the Masses from being washed away by the Dream of Space, the Dream of a Better Future. The Union was instrumental in killing the Dream of Space and, if the Union had not interfered, the Dream of Space would have caused the return of the Dreaming and the strengthening of the sense of wonder of the world. Instead of embracing the Dream of Space, the Union drowned humanity in accounting tricks and bureaucratic nightmares, seeking to kill the Dream of Space with Banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T14:35:58-08:00","id":1038582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038205#post1038205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's more a sliding scale from Flash Gordon to 2001: A Space Odyssey</div> </div> </div> </div>Was going to quote your earlier but this one works even better. There can be a lot of Banality even in Star Trek, for example, everyone is dressed the same and even have colors to denote what they do. Star Wars can have the mythical force until it is explained with midiclorians, or however you spell it. Now for a Mage reference SoE are not as banal as ItX but they still want to define to much. Could go ona bit longer but I would begin to ramble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T14:53:57-08:00","id":1038596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038554#post1038554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Union seeks to limit and to regulate magic, they are more bureaucrats and accountants than they are scientists. Science is actually something that the Union is not too found of because Science is a hydra (for every question that is answered, two more are spawned). In fact, most magical traditions have been experimental and scientific in their approach throughout history, as magicians and witches have always sought wonder and strived for understanding.<br /> <br /> While people may claim that we have advanced plenty in the last fifty years, the greatest scientific achievement in history was the Apollo Mission. Everything developed since then has been a distraction to prevent the Banality of the Masses from being washed away by the Dream of Space, the Dream of a Better Future. The Union was instrumental in killing the Dream of Space and, if the Union had not interfered, the Dream of Space would have caused the return of the Dreaming and the strengthening of the sense of wonder of the world. Instead of embracing the Dream of Space, the Union drowned humanity in accounting tricks and bureaucratic nightmares, seeking to kill the Dream of Space with Banality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought that the Union wanted the Dream of Space? I remember reading that even though they &quot;won&quot; the Ascension War, they ended up losing as well. That humanity had become so Banal that they couldn't introduce the new ships and wonders on their schedule, because humanity's belief was stuck firmly in &quot;end of history&quot; mode and they couldn't entertain all the awesome stuff that the Union had planned for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T15:10:07-08:00","id":1038602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038513#post1038513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Union doesn't dream of the future; in Mage, it has it on a schedule, and in other games, it probably still has some kind of strict regulatory plan in place, to the extent that it can manage in a crossover setting. Step off the schedule or disrupt the plan, and you get removed (killing people will net you temporary Banality, so if you're fine with disappearing people for the sake of a conspiracy, you probably have a lot of it).</div> </div> </div> </div>A schedule that's fucked up due to Banality. Something most technocrats don't acknowledge nor understand. This was actually my Iterators reasoning for trying to develop an acceptable means for changelings to enter the consensus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038554#post1038554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Union seeks to limit and to regulate magic, they are more bureaucrats and accountants than they are scientists. Science is actually something that the Union is not too found of because Science is a hydra (for every question that is answered, two more are spawned). In fact, most magical traditions have been experimental and scientific in their approach throughout history, as magicians and witches have always sought wonder and strived for understanding.<br /> <br /> While people may claim that we have advanced plenty in the last fifty years, the greatest scientific achievement in history was the Apollo Mission. Everything developed since then has been a distraction to prevent the Banality of the Masses from being washed away by the Dream of Space, the Dream of a Better Future. The Union was instrumental in killing the Dream of Space and, if the Union had not interfered, the Dream of Space would have caused the return of the Dreaming and the strengthening of the sense of wonder of the world. Instead of embracing the Dream of Space, the Union drowned humanity in accounting tricks and bureaucratic nightmares, seeking to kill the Dream of Space with Banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Union seeks to limit and regulate reality itself. Largely because science is invalid in the world of Mage the Ascension. Science depends upon the fact that reality has set rules, and those rules do not change over time. Circumstances within the construct that runs off of those rules may change, but the rules themselves are eternal.<br /> <br /> This fact is laughably, horribly false in Mage. There are no set rules. There are only the infinite possibilities and insane whims of consensus. There is no outer truth that can be discovered by scientific experimentation. Even the 'rules' of the game of Mage is merely a second consensus that the awakened keep to. One that allows themselves greater freedom than the masses of course, but still has limits. Is still safe.<br /> <br /> If you want a true look at reality. Look at the Marauders. The worst of the Marauders, the ones so far gone that their reality connects with yours at no point. THAT. Is what reality is. Deep down inside.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy denies this. The Technocracy does their best to build a lie that will stand forever. To construct a universal set of laws. With no exceptions, with no tricks. With none of the maddening infinite possibility of the world they live in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T15:22:15-08:00","id":1038607,"title":"","content":"The Union denies the Dream of Space. In the 1960s, the US government rejected the Sea Dragon in favor of smaller spacecraft designs because someone wanted to deny access to space to the Masses. In the 1970s, NASA was forced to abandon its plans for Orbital Power Satellites, Moon Mines, and Mars Colonies (all of which could have been done with the existing technology) because someone wanted to deny the benefits of space to the Masses. With each decade, someone denied the Dream of Space to the Masses and, since the Technocrats were shaping the Concensus, they are the only ones who could have denied the Dream of Space to the Masses. The Union is not controlled by scientists, it is controlled by accountants and bureaucrats who abuse science to create a world where the majority of humans have no hopes or dreams, just pain and suffering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T15:31:23-08:00","id":1038611,"title":"","content":"The Union is hardly controlled by accountants and Bureaucrats.<br /> <br /> It's controlled by Economists and Psychologists. It's controlled by Engineers and Geneticists and Dimensional Scientists.. The union believes in science, but not so much the scientific method. The unions goal is a perfect world. One where there is no need for change, and any change from the blueprint would only make things worse.<br /> <br /> They write the laws of physics and enforce them, as any lawmaker does. And they write them the way they do for the benefit of all. They right the wrongs of the world as it stands, building a new, better one to take it's place. Are there problems? Of course there are. They're hardly finished. They're nowhere even CLOSE to finished. And any reconstruction can only happen once people stop <i>fighting them.</i> The people cannot reap the benefits of Unity, because the war, despite what some people think, is not over. Or even close to over. The war won't be over until noone is left to oppose the union. Until noone will attempt to take the unions gifts to all humanity and turn them into weapons of war to destroy any hope of Unity.<br /> <br /> It's better to tear the whole thing to the ground, then to build upon a flawed foundation. And the foundation is still very much flawed. Unity, and the utopia it represents, can only be built when humanity embraces it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T16:11:53-08:00","id":1038630,"title":"","content":"The Syndicate is nothing but mobsters with accounting degrees and NWO is nothing but bureaucrats with business degrees. The rest of the Union is similarly banal. The promise of the Union is a lie, a lie that hides the truth, that the Union exists only for the benefit of the Enlightened, and the Unenlightened are merely tools to be used until they break, when they are thrown away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T16:31:26-08:00","id":1038636,"title":"","content":"Firstly, the NWO doesn't do business. NWO does politics and psychology. The Syndicate literally built the modern economy an economic system that provides peace and plenty to millions of people.<br /> <br /> The Union exists, and solely exists, for the benefit of all. There are the corrupt. Those who use the union as a tool to feed their own hunger power and position. But they are eliminated as found. All operatives of the union are tools. Enlightened and unenlightened both. Tools glad to be used to build a better world.<br /> <br /> What alternative is there? The foolishness of the Traditions and their old boys club? The petty childishness of the Disparates? Neither have the capability nor the desire to make a world worth living in. The Traditions would sell you a vision of a world divided up into feifdoms. Competing paradigms spread across the whole planet separate but equal. But such a thing is a pipe dream, and worse a danger to everyone on the planet. People cannot believe two things, they cannot accept two, opposing things to be true. This is apparent even amongst their ranks. As the traditions seperate themselves by paradigm. There might be some level of cultural cross contamination. But it's not a true blending.<br /> <br /> In attempting to sustain all paradigms, they will instead invalidate all paradigms... Opening the floodgates of new paradigms, and thus the potential for the world and it's people to be destroyed increases. Given time, any non-zero chance of the world being destroyed by an apocalyptic paradigm becomes a statistical inevitability.<br /> <br /> And the Disparates, are barely even coherent in their goals. They're petty thugs with petty grievances, incapable of seeing the forest for the trees. That they managed to become enlightened at all is a shock. Given how they can't see basic universal truths are a necessity if any of us are to survive.<br /> <br /> No. Humanities last, best, and only hope is in the Technocratic Union. The world is terrible, this is true. But it is not terrible because they want it to be. It is terrible because it must be. Because despite the proclamations of victory, we have but won the first battle of the ascension war. We live in the ruins of a terrible civilization and things will only get worse before the future gets better. But there is hope, and there always will be hope. Hope for a better tomorrow. A tomorrow where the war is won. where Humanity is united in true consensus for the first time in history.<br /> <br /> And on that day. Unity will be won.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Do I get the job as the local Union Propagandist yet?)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T16:47:26-08:00","id":1038646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038630#post1038630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Syndicate is nothing but mobsters with accounting degrees and NWO is nothing but bureaucrats with business degrees. The rest of the Union is similarly banal. The promise of the Union is a lie, a lie that hides the truth, that the Union exists only for the benefit of the Enlightened, and the Unenlightened are merely tools to be used until they break, when they are thrown away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your use of absolutes makes your technocracy pretty 1 dimensional in my opinion.<br /> <br /> For me, I'd say yes, Syndicate has a lot of mobsters within their ranks, but for the most part they are consultants, they own companies, they measure the stock market, they travel the world telling people how the global economy works as they constantly test out their theories of Prime in accordance with what the Timetable demands. They are the entrepreneurs who only want Humanity to be satisfied with what they give them.<br /> <br /> The NWO is much more involved that Bureaucrats with Business degrees. They are the Men in Black, the government agents at your door. They are the sociologists and psychologists that can get you to tell them whatever they want to hear from you with a little lite coercion. These are the people listening to your calls, processing your accounts, following your paper trails. They are Big Brother, they know exactly where you've been and what your doing, they only ask to see how you will answer They are the village and you are No. 6. They are the internet, they are the world.<br /> But they are also the teachers, the historians, the academics who ensure that everyone thinks correctly, they will tell you what to think and how to think it or else you won't get that degree that proves what a good little sleeper you are.<br /> <br /> However, As black and white as the union would prefer things to be (especially the NWO), each agent, each employee is an individual who has their own reasons for doing the things they do. Some are idealists who trulley believe what they are doing is for the benefit of mankind, some are optimists who think that the union can improve over time if enough work is done, some are just in it for the power, others have no choice. Still, there may be a few agents that were seduced by the excitement of the job, the lfestyle, of just being &quot;in the club&quot; so to speak. Some are doing this because they are scared of what a world without the Technocracy would look like.<br /> <br /> No two Technocrats have the same ambitions either, some may want to clamber to the top of the heap, others are in it only for the science, to discover new revolutionary technology that can benefit their fellow man without need for superhuman powers. There will be those that actually do it all for job security, the union can be a very comfortable place for those who just want a steady paycheck with a couple added perks for keeping secrets and not asking too many questions. Some, however, have something to prove, either to themselves or their superiors, they have a vision they the Union's help with to make into reality. There are even those who just have fun with it, all they want to do is build for no other reason than because they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T20:06:33-08:00","id":1038723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038630#post1038630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Syndicate is nothing but mobsters with accounting degrees and NWO is nothing but bureaucrats with business degrees. The rest of the Union is similarly banal. The promise of the Union is a lie, a lie that hides the truth, that the Union exists only for the benefit of the Enlightened, and the Unenlightened are merely tools to be used until they break, when they are thrown away.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet they've given us so many wonderful things. Take a look outside your window, and notice all the conveniences of modern technology. Indoor plumbing, antibiotics, and Taco Bell. Also notice that people aren't the slaves of wizards living in ivory towers who incinerate entire villages with fireballs if one of the peasants living in a hut made of dung accidentally stains his ermine robe with filth? Have you thanked a Technocrat today?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T20:31:18-08:00","id":1038735,"title":"","content":"We know who invented each of those miracles. Yes, the Union takes credit for the progress of technology, but I posit that they are merely magical parasites that take credit for the hard work and genius of the Masses. For example, indoor plumbing dates back to a minimum of the 17th century BC. At best, they are responsible for the popularization of questionable economic theories like trickle-down economics and social media platforms that have encouraged cyber bullying and the spread of white nationalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T21:03:37-08:00","id":1038745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038735#post1038735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At best, they are responsible for the popularization of questionable economic theories like trickle-down economics and social media platforms that have encouraged cyber bullying and the spread of white nationalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and Norman Borlaug. If you don't know who Norman Borlaug is, you're like most people. But the shorthand version is that he was a biologist specializing in food sciences whose personal contributions to the Green Revolution in agriculture saved a billion human beings from dying of starvation. That is billion with a b. He started out saving more human lives than you or I ever will by working on developing new strains of wheat in Mexico. It took more than a dozen years of hand-cross pollination, growing in a variety of soil types and water conditions, compiling his data and progressively increasing disease resistance. The man's work exuded enough banality to kill an Arcadian dragon at a hundred paces...<br /> <br /> ...but it worked. If the man wasn't a Technocrat, then he used their methods. And he was a product of the public education system of the United States that grew out of the Technocratic-backed Enlightenment-era philosophy. He practiced a branch of science codified by the Progenitors. He bought into the scientific paradigm that applied genetics, plant breeding, plant pathology, entomology, agronomy, soil science, and cereal sciences could make the world a better place by, you know, feeding a billion hungry people.<br /> <br /> Hit me with the greatest hero to come out of the Traditions. How many lives has he or she saved? What lasting impact has he or she had on the world? Tell you what. Give me the best five heroes to come out of the Traditions and tell me how many lives they've saved. If it comes close to a billion, let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T21:27:35-08:00","id":1038754,"title":"","content":"The Green Revolution allowed the population of the Earth to grow from 3 billion to 7.5 billion and, due to increased resource consumption from that population, led to countless extinct species, the increased suffering of billions of people, and the potential annihilation of 95% of humanity before 2100 due to global climate change. He might as well have been Nephandi for the damage and suffering that his 'revolution' has caused over the past fifty years and will cause over the next fifty years. Higher populations are not better populations when you do not have the resources to provide for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T21:58:26-08:00","id":1038766,"title":"","content":"There seems to be a presumption that Glamour is unalloyed Goodness and Sweetness and Niceness, the call of banality is humanity reacting to the pain and suffering, the horrors that the Dreaming can provide. Banality is SAFE. That's the promise of the Technocracy, &quot;You won't get eaten by Dragons. unfortunately we have to kill a bunch of unicorns to get there.&quot; The Traditions argue &quot;Unicorns are worth the occasional person getting eaten by Dragons&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> That's what it boils down to for all the methodologies and what have you the question is about Safety vs Freedom. There is nothing intrinsically banal about technology or understanding or what have you the Technocracy has made an active choice to help make the world more hostile to alien body stealing Parasites. That these Alien body stealing parasites happen to be fairies and they happen to live in dreams and that it happens to make humanity less in some fashion is the price the Technocracy is willing to pay so that fewer people are Eaten by Redcaps.<br /> <br /> Everything else is just arguing semantics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T22:09:04-08:00","id":1038768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038766#post1038766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There seems to be a presumption that Glamour is unalloyed Goodness and Sweetness and Niceness, the call of banality is humanity reacting to the pain and suffering, the horrors that the Dreaming can provide. Banality is SAFE. That's the promise of the Technocracy, &quot;You won't get eaten by Dragons. unfortunately we have to kill a bunch of unicorns to get there.&quot; The Traditions argue &quot;Unicorns are worth the occasional person getting eaten by Dragons&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, even Unicorns are hardly pleasant. Back in the day, unicorns weren't seen as gentle creatures that modern sentimentality paints them, but wild, dangerous beasts. Noble, in their own way, but still dangerous. It's telling that on certain English coats of arms, where the lion and the unicorn stood side by side, it was the <i>unicorn</i> depicted in chains, to bind its wild nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T05:58:47-08:00","id":1038850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038754#post1038754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Green Revolution allowed the population of the Earth to grow from 3 billion to 7.5 billion and, due to increased resource consumption from that population, led to countless extinct species, the increased suffering of billions of people, and the potential annihilation of 95% of humanity before 2100 due to global climate change. He might as well have been Nephandi for the damage and suffering that his 'revolution' has caused over the past fifty years and will cause over the next fifty years. Higher populations are not better populations when you do not have the resources to provide for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Green Revolution is a bad thing.&quot; Spoken like a person who's never known hunger. Take care now you crazy kids!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T06:36:10-08:00","id":1038861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038745#post1038745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...and Norman Borlaug. If you don't know who Norman Borlaug is, you're like most people. But the shorthand version is that he was a biologist specializing in food sciences whose personal contributions to the Green Revolution in agriculture saved a billion human beings from dying of starvation. That is billion with a b. He started out saving more human lives than you or I ever will by working on developing new strains of wheat in Mexico. It took more than a dozen years of hand-cross pollination, growing in a variety of soil types and water conditions, compiling his data and progressively increasing disease resistance. The man's work exuded enough banality to kill an Arcadian dragon at a hundred paces...<br /> <br /> ...but it worked. If the man wasn't a Technocrat, then he used their methods. And he was a product of the public education system of the United States that grew out of the Technocratic-backed Enlightenment-era philosophy. He practiced a branch of science codified by the Progenitors. He bought into the scientific paradigm that applied genetics, plant breeding, plant pathology, entomology, agronomy, soil science, and cereal sciences could make the world a better place by, you know, feeding a billion hungry people.<br /> <br /> Hit me with the greatest hero to come out of the Traditions. How many lives has he or she saved? What lasting impact has he or she had on the world? Tell you what. Give me the best five heroes to come out of the Traditions and tell me how many lives they've saved. If it comes close to a billion, let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Argh, you've put me in such a hard spot, because Borlaug did amazing humanitarian and scientific work and the similarities are there but I really don't want to use him a a picture of the Technocracy. So let me say this, if Norman Borlaug is an example of the Technocracy at its best, Trofim Lysenko represents it at its worst; working in the name of the people, but willing to let millions die rather than use methods they don't approve of. Unworkable ideas forced on the masses by the might of the academic elite and the state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T06:40:15-08:00","id":1038862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038861#post1038861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Argh, you've put me in such a hard spot, because Borlaug did amazing humanitarian and scientific work and the similarities are there but I really don't want to use him a a picture of the Technocracy. So let me say this, if Norman Borlaug is an example of the Technocracy at its best, Trofim Lysenko represents it at its worst; working in the name of the people, but willing to let millions die rather than use methods they don't approve of. Unworkable ideas forced on the masses by the might of the academic elite and the state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dogmatic adherence to ideology isn't a unique trait among Technocrats. Paging Torquemada.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T06:53:51-08:00","id":1038866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038862#post1038862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dogmatic adherence to ideology isn't a unique trait among Technocrats. Paging Torquemada.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are absolutely right, and neither are humanitarian efforts. But the particular combination of Government backed Science crushing the opposition is as emblematic of the Technocracy as the methodical and targetted engineering Borlaug practiced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T07:09:36-08:00","id":1038873,"title":"","content":"So in conclusion. There are technocratic idealists as well as technocratic exploiters. It's all a bit of a soup.<br /> <br /> Which makes sense, because I've always seen the Technocracy as a short hand reflection and commentary on the state of real life society and its many angles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T07:30:28-08:00","id":1038881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038866#post1038866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are absolutely right, and neither are humanitarian efforts. But the particular combination of Government backed Science crushing the opposition is as emblematic of the Technocracy as the methodical and targetted engineering Borlaug practiced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but my point was that when you pair the humanitarianism of Borlaug with the methods of the Technocracy, you net a billion lives saved. What's the best outcome if you pair the same humanitarian impulses with the methods of the Traditions? Does it even come close to an appreciable fraction of a billion lives saved from hunger?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T07:36:10-08:00","id":1038883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038754#post1038754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Green Revolution allowed the population of the Earth to grow from 3 billion to 7.5 billion and, due to increased resource consumption from that population, led to countless extinct species, the increased suffering of billions of people, and the potential annihilation of 95% of humanity before 2100 due to global climate change. He might as well have been Nephandi for the damage and suffering that his 'revolution' has caused over the past fifty years and will cause over the next fifty years. Higher populations are not better populations when you do not have the resources to provide for them.</div> </div> </div> </div> What? This line of thinking is almost a textbook rational for what a Nephandi might think. &quot;I need to save the world by destroying it. Only by culling most of the human population and enslaving it can we ensure they are truly happy.&quot; Well, maybe that's just Red Talon, actually.<br /> <br /> And Ben, on that note, I assume the answer would be, 'if everyone could just do magic, they'd have been able to fix the world hunger issue themselves.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T07:39:32-08:00","id":1038888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038883#post1038883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Ben, on that note, I assume the answer would be, 'if everyone could just do magic, they'd have been able to fix the world hunger issue themselves.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone CAN do magic under the Technocracy. Today I used a Correspondance/Prime rote to make sure that I have access to warmth (Forces) and the means to cook my food (Matter) for the next month. I paid my gas bill on my cell phone.<br /> <br /> The Traditions had from the first Awakened Avatar to the 14th century to progress towards universal use of magic. Then the Order of Reason was founded, and flash forward less than a millennium later. <b>*looks around and picks up the telephone*</b> &quot;Technocracy? This is the Traditions. You win.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":1515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","user":"BenjCano","date":". 01-27-2017, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T07:47:47-08:00","id":1038891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038881#post1038881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, but my point was that when you pair the humanitarianism of Borlaug with the methods of the Technocracy, you net a billion lives saved. What's the best outcome if you pair the same humanitarian impulses with the methods of the Traditions? Does it even come close to an appreciable fraction of a billion lives saved from hunger?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard to say, because you have to use times and situations when the Traditions had the power to do that, and those are few and far between. You'd also have to adjust for the population size they could affect at those times. Lysenko didn't starve nearly as many people as Borlaug fed, but he didn't have access to as many either.<br /> <br /> Also in Mage, some Mages have literally saved the world. So there are a number of them who have a higher Saved count than Borlaug.<br /> <br /> But I think the question of what the Technocracy is like at its best <i>and</i> worst is actually the most relevant thing to the discussion, because the organization can embody both the fondest dreams and the foulest nightmares of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T07:57:43-08:00","id":1038895,"title":"","content":"We would have experienced the growth in global GDP from 1960-2015 without the extra 4.5 billion people because they just represent subsistence farmers and the urban self-employed (we could actually maintain our civilization with just 1 billion people, but that is a different argument). While the standard of living would likely be unchanged in the developed world, the standard of living in the developing world would have likely been 2.5 times higher. The average nominal income in the developing world would be $17,500 instead of $5,000, which would be 50% of average developed world nominal incomes instead of 15%. Everyone would be wealthier, the environmental would be cleaner, and the world would be a better place.<br /> <br /> If we had promoted reproductive freedoms for women along with the Green Revolution, we could have saved the starving Masses as well as allowed women to have the choice of how many children they wanted. While some would have continued to have eight children, most would have stopped at two children. Without reproductive freedoms for women, however, the Green Revolution helped to create the monstrous population growth of humanity. <br /> <br /> The end result has been the cancerous growth of humanity and the death spiral of the global ecosystem. Humanity will experience a die off before 2100, the only question is whether we will die back to 3 billion or if we will die back to 300 million. I doubt that the Technocrats can do much to stop it, as they have done nothing to promote beneficial technologies like fusion energy or space industry, just technologies that increase the banality and suffering of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T08:04:05-08:00","id":1038899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038895#post1038895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We would have experienced the growth in global GDP from 1960-2015 without the extra 4.5 billion people because they just represent subsistence farmers and the urban self-employed (we could actually maintain our civilization with just 1 billion people, but that is a different argument). While the standard of living would likely be unchanged in the developed world, the standard of living in the developing world would have likely been 2.5 times higher. The average nominal income in the developing world would be $17,500 instead of $5,000, which would be 50% of average developed world nominal incomes instead of 15%. Everyone would be wealthier, the environmental would be cleaner, and the world would be a better place.<br /> <br /> If we had promoted reproductive freedoms for women along with the Green Revolution, we could have saved the starving Masses as well as allowed women to have the choice of how many children they wanted. While some would have continued to have eight children, most would have stopped at two children. Without reproductive freedoms for women, however, the Green Revolution helped to create the monstrous population growth of humanity.<br /> <br /> The end result has been the cancerous growth of humanity and the death spiral of the global ecosystem. Humanity will experience a die off before 2100, the only question is whether we will die back to 3 billion or if we will die back to 300 million. I doubt that the Technocrats can do much to stop it, as they have done nothing to promote beneficial technologies like fusion energy or space industry, just technologies that increase the banality and suffering of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to mentally substitute &quot;the hungry&quot; with &quot;the poor&quot; as I watch this video:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=owI7DOeO_yg&amp;ab_channel=Dvdmitch\" data-code=\"owI7DOeO_yg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/owI7DOeO_yg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T08:09:28-08:00","id":1038903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038888#post1038888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone CAN do magic under the Technocracy. Today I used a Correspondance/Prime rote to make sure that I have access to warmth (Forces) and the means to cook my food (Matter) for the next month. I paid my gas bill on my cell phone.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, as I said, the argument of the Traditions would be, 'like what happened, but better.' That increased influence of reality under individuals would be better for more humanity than the more predictable methods of the Union.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Traditions had from the first Awakened Avatar to the 14th century to progress towards universal use of magic. Then the Order of Reason was founded, and flash forward less than a millennium later. <b>*looks around and picks up the telephone*</b> &quot;Technocracy? This is the Traditions. You win.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Eh, not really organized before that point. And let's not pretend that millennium didn't have massive problems and suffering.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T08:14:35-08:00","id":1038905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038861#post1038861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Argh, you've put me in such a hard spot, because Borlaug did amazing humanitarian and scientific work and the similarities are there but I really don't want to use him a a picture of the Technocracy. So let me say this, if Norman Borlaug is an example of the Technocracy at its best, Trofim Lysenko represents it at its worst; working in the name of the people, but willing to let millions die rather than use methods they don't approve of. Unworkable ideas forced on the masses by the might of the academic elite and the state.</div> </div> </div> </div>By Mage standards Lysenko is an influential etherite - they are the ones gathering pseudoscientists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T08:28:00-08:00","id":1038915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038905#post1038905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By Mage standards Lysenko is an influential etherite - they are the ones gathering pseudoscientists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, that's just propaganda from the organization that still uses killer cyborgs and psychic powers against its enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T08:44:26-08:00","id":1038922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, not really organized before that point. And let's not pretend that millennium didn't have massive problems and suffering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. The Traditions formed in response to the Order of Reason. Blaming anything from before on them it's not just. After all, it was a group of idealistic Hermetics who founded the Order.<br /> In truth, it's not that older mages &quot;failed in protecting the masses&quot;, but rather than such issue wasn't even asked before the Craftmasons. Their founding ideals, based partly on the pesdestal in which the old Hermetics put the human race (created as inheritors of the power of god and all that), were the foundation of a new world, and brought up a Paradigm Shift that produced not only the greatest idealist among the Technocracy, but also the most &quot;socialy acceptable&quot; face of the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T09:51:16-08:00","id":1038952,"title":"","content":"The Union claims to rule the world, so it must accept responsibility for the suffering caused over the past century. It cannot just claim responsibility for the 'good' technologies, especially since it has suppressed fusion energy, reproductive freedom, and space colonization. The fact that it only claims the good while ignoring the bad just makes it a parasite that exploits the Masses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T09:53:17-08:00","id":1038953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038922#post1038922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very true. The Traditions formed in response to the Order of Reason. Blaming anything from before on them it's not just. After all, it was a group of idealistic Hermetics who founded the Order.<br /> In truth, it's not that older mages &quot;failed in protecting the masses&quot;, but rather than such issue wasn't even asked before the Craftmasons. Their founding ideals, based partly on the pesdestal in which the old Hermetics put the human race (created as inheritors of the power of god and all that), were the foundation of a new world, and brought up a Paradigm Shift that produced not only the greatest idealist among the Technocracy, but also the most &quot;socialy acceptable&quot; face of the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last time I checked, the ideal of the old Hermetics was that only the worthy can have the power and rights, and that only Hermetics are worthy. The founding of the Order of Hermes in the 9th century wasn't followed by the Renaissance - that was five hundred years later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T09:57:34-08:00","id":1038955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038952#post1038952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Union claims to rule the world, so it must accept responsibility for the suffering caused over the past century. It cannot just claim responsibility for the 'good' technologies, especially since it has suppressed fusion energy, reproductive freedom, and <b>space colonization</b>. The fact that it only claims the good while ignoring the bad just makes it a parasite that exploits the Masses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about the first two so let's focus on the last one. In Mage Space as we know it doesn't exist. It's actually Umbra. Getting on a spaceship and flying away from Earth is a magic feat and if your ship has muggles on it - it explodes. So give it time. The consensus will catch up and Spirit 3 will become mundane reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T10:35:28-08:00","id":1038975,"title":"","content":"Actually they can and do colonize space. Prior to the DA there were more humans in void colonies than on earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T11:09:57-08:00","id":1038987,"title":"","content":"But we do not need to wait for the Consensus because the technology for space colonization has existed since the 1960s (ever since the first flight of the Apollo Program). NASA has had the technology since the 1960s for Orbital Power Satellites, Moon Mines, Mars Colonies, etc. The only thing that has prevented space colonization has been political opposition, not technological difficulties, so the Consensus does not matter because the technologies have existed for fifty years. It is the opposition of the Union (through its control and influence over the political process) that is the only thing in cWoD that kept the Masses from space colonization because it fear the Dream of Space (and I would like a book and page number for the population of the void colonies if you would not mind).<br /> <br /> And when we are talking about crossovers, the Consensus is nothing but a magical artifact (fueled by the suffering over an ever increasing human population) that was created by the Technocracy in order to commit mass genocide against the magical creatures of Reality. In a crossover, Outer Space is Outer Space, Reality is Reality, and Science is Science, and the Technocracy is a genocidal order whose goals make the Nazis seem unambitious. In fact, the only difference between the Nephandi and the Technocracy is that the Nephandi are more honest with themselves about their eventual goals while the Technocracy uses double speak and mind control to keep its members from understanding the evils that they are committing.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Outer Space, only Mages are incapable of accessing the Deep Umbra within the Asteroid Belt and only Mages are incapable of accessing Outer Space beyond the Asteroid Belt. Fera are capable of visiting three levels of Outer Space (the Aetherial Realm, the Deep Umbra, and Outer Space) and, through traveling the Roads of Balor from the Dreaming, the Changelings are capable of similar explorations of Outer Space as the Fera. It is the beliefs of the Mages that prevent them from exploring as much of Reality as the Fera and the Changelings (and the Changelings get to explore the Dreaming as well).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T11:24:03-08:00","id":1038997,"title":"","content":"Aya, remember that &quot;technology exists&quot; and &quot;technology reliably works&quot; are not the same in Mage. Firearms exist in Sorcerer's Crusade. But if you send an expedition into America - they stop working and become a pure Forces effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038987#post1038987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a crossover, Outer Space is Outer Space, Reality is Reality, and Science is Science</div> </div> </div> </div>Top kek. Read Rage Across Russia. You'll learn that Space Station MIR is actually a breeding ground of the Black Spiral Dancers and Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T11:28:41-08:00","id":1039004,"title":"","content":"But that does not apply in a crossover, which is the point when you are comparing Changelings and Mages (firearms worked for the first Changelings and Garou that invaded the Americas with the Spanish Conquistadors and I really doubt that they were using Forces). Yes, the Black Spiral Dancers cross over from the Aetherial Realm (or the Deep Umbra) into Outer Space where the MIR was located (it was not really a breeding ground, as the MIR was too small, but more of a place of entertainment).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"k