er tight quarters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:43:15-08:00","id":1039055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1038754#post1038754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Green Revolution allowed the population of the Earth to grow from 3 billion to 7.5 billion and, due to increased resource consumption from that population, led to countless extinct species, the increased suffering of billions of people, and the potential annihilation of 95% of humanity before 2100 due to global climate change. He might as well have been Nephandi for the damage and suffering that his 'revolution' has caused over the past fifty years and will cause over the next fifty years. Higher populations are not better populations when you do not have the resources to provide for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The agricultural revolution about 10.000 years ago allowed for the growth of the human populations to a scale beyond compare previously, and that's what allowed for the rise of civilization. <br /> <br /> It also the advancement that invented war.<br