approved of the development of Wahhabi terrorism by encouraging the Western governments to ignore the fact that our allies in the Gulf were funding Wahhabi terrorists.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question you're not asking here is..... <i>why?</i><br /> <br /> You mention atrocities and then just.... stop there. You don't think for one moment about why. The union never does anything without a reason. They have no spirits or gods to appease, every act of theirs is a calculated move intended to net them some future advantage.<br /> <br /> So <i>why</i> did they overthrow 'democratically elected' governments? <i>Why</i> would they encourage Wahhabi terrorists? Both are certainly within the Unions power, and I can even see a reason for both within the unions ideology.<br /> <br /> So, what's the <i>reason.</i> Theirs is the paradigm <b>of</b> reason after all. Surely they have one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T16:34:27-08:00","id":1039152,"title":"","content":"This is one of those moments where my stance in Mage is very different than my stance in real life. Because I will fight like hell to keep the Traditions and the Technocracy as morally compromised heroes, but in real life I have to side with technology and democracy all the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T16:41:05-08:00","id":1039155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039147#post1039147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No no, that's where your wrong. The Traditions DO want freedom. It's just that to a Hermetic, 'freedom' is the ability to fireball a peasant in the face on a whim. And he's got his huevos all twisted up because the Technocracy is trying to keep him from doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just the Hermetics<br /> <br /> Freedom to the Euthanatos: freedom to &quot;purify the unworth&quot;<br /> Freedom to the Celestial Chorus: same as Euthanatos<br /> Freedom to the Dreamspeakers: freedom to turn their people into slaves of spirits (with them holding the whips)<br /> Freedom to the Virtual Adepts: irresponsible anarch<br /> Freedom to the Verbena: freedom to do their orgies and blood sacrifices<br /> Freedom to the Cult of Ecstasy: to be free of any responsability<br /> Freedom to the Akashic: freedom to meditate upon the meanings of a falling leaf or bird flying. Not that bad... But also don't care about the sleepers<br /> Freedom to the Etherites: well, those we can at least tolerate, they actually DO wanna something good for all and not just themselves (and we have to admit that they hold many of the good that the Union lost. But that's the price the Union had to pay, to conquer the world, we had to lose our souls. Goodbye brothers, its a shame it had to be like this)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T16:55:26-08:00","id":1039159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039155#post1039155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Freedom to the Akashic: freedom to meditate upon the meanings of a falling leaf or bird flying. Not that bad... But also don't care about the sleepers</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to look at what the Akashic think of sleepers, I think we can turn to a look at Tibet, which is ruled by a divinely appointed heavenly monarch who rules as an absolute tyrant at the Tibetan community in exile, has banned oral and anal sex as well as masturbation, and wants to return to the feudal domination of the elite priestly class that the first foreign visitors to the country were compelled to observe were hideously oppressive with brutal execution and hideous punishment for violating the edicts of the lamas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T17:07:44-08:00","id":1039167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039155#post1039155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Freedom to the Etherites: well, those we can at least tolerate, they actually DO wanna something good for all and not just themselves (and we have to admit that they hold many of the good that the Union lost. But that's the price the Union had to pay, to conquer the world, we had to lose our souls. Goodbye brothers, its a shame it had to be like this)</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I don't think the Etherites would be so benevolent. They'd be groups of scientists constantly trying to one-up each other with more and more elaborate shows of genius.<br /> But worse than that, there would be a geniocratic oligarcy where only the intelligent would be taken seriously. This may sound good on paper, but it's basically the same set up as the Hermetics, but with cogs, gears, and zappers in place of books, symbols, and staves. Imagine, your entire worth to society depending on how good you were in the lab, how creative you were in the inventors workshop. All others shunned to second class citizens.<br /> If you were strong but of average intelligence, you might get work as a labourer, but good luck ever amounting to much more or being seen as anything more than a dumb oaf. Everyone else, however, what need is there of you?<br /> You would have to demonstrate your intelligence for the right to vote, protest, or speak in a public forum, we can't have the rabble ruining our clockwork community now can we?<br /> You'd have to work damn hard to be seen above the naturally gifted. If someone has a higher IQ than you, you can bet they'll be getting preferential treatment in almost any avenue. They'll just be &quot;better&quot; after all.<br /> And you better be kind and supporting towards their work. Some of those etherites can get a tad touchy about their latest inventions, and won't take kindly to a stupid oaf telling them giving them advice. Say the wrong thing and you may just become the perfect candidate to test out their prototype.<br /> So smile and nod, say &quot;Yes professor&quot; and &quot;Of course, you're the scientist&quot; and be on your way. And you better get out of the way before the airship battle starts. If you die in their combat, it's your fault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T17:07:58-08:00","id":1039168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039151#post1039151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question you're not asking here is..... <i>why?</i><br /> <br /> You mention atrocities and then just.... stop there. You don't think for one moment about why. The union never does anything without a reason. They have no spirits or gods to appease, every act of theirs is a calculated move intended to net them some future advantage.<br /> <br /> So <i>why</i> did they overthrow 'democratically elected' governments? <i>Why</i> would they encourage Wahhabi terrorists? Both are certainly within the Unions power, and I can even see a reason for both within the unions ideology.<br /> <br /> So, what's the <i>reason.</i> Theirs is the paradigm <b>of</b> reason after all. Surely they have one?</div> </div> </div> </div>To increase the number of people who can be exploited by the West. With lower populations and higher incomes, the developing world would have been less vulnerable to the corporate exploitation that leads to environmental degradation and labor abuses. They do not want to improve the Masses, they just want to exploit the Masses, and they are willing to destroy or kill anything that threatens their exploitation of the Masses. Otherwise, we would have publicly known Asteroid/Moon Mines, Orbital Colonies, and Solar Power Satellites (as well as a wealthier, if smaller, population).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T17:13:50-08:00","id":1039169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039168#post1039168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To increase the number of people who can be exploited by the West. With lower populations and higher incomes, the developing world would have been less vulnerable to the corporate exploitation that leads to environmental degradation and labor abuses. They do not want to improve the Masses, they just want to exploit the Masses, and they are willing to destroy or kill anything that threatens their exploitation of the Masses. Otherwise, we would have publicly known Asteroid/Moon Mines, Orbital Colonies, and Solar Power Satellites (as well as a wealthier, if smaller, population).</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoken like a Tradition Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T17:48:59-08:00","id":1039178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039167#post1039167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I don't think the Etherites would be so benevolent. They'd be groups of scientists constantly trying to one-up each other with more and more elaborate shows of genius.<br /> But worse than that, there would be a geniocratic oligarcy where only the intelligent would be taken seriously. This may sound good on paper, but it's basically the same set up as the Hermetics, but with cogs, gears, and zappers in place of books, symbols, and staves. Imagine, your entire worth to society depending on how good you were in the lab, how creative you were in the inventors workshop. All others shunned to second class citizens.<br /> If you were strong but of average intelligence, you might get work as a labourer, but good luck ever amounting to much more or being seen as anything more than a dumb oaf. Everyone else, however, what need is there of you?<br /> You would have to demonstrate your intelligence for the right to vote, protest, or speak in a public forum, we can't have the rabble ruining our clockwork community now can we?<br /> You'd have to work damn hard to be seen above the naturally gifted. If someone has a higher IQ than you, you can bet they'll be getting preferential treatment in almost any avenue. They'll just be &quot;better&quot; after all.<br /> And you better be kind and supporting towards their work. Some of those etherites can get a tad touchy about their latest inventions, and won't take kindly to a stupid oaf telling them giving them advice. Say the wrong thing and you may just become the perfect candidate to test out their prototype.<br /> So smile and nod, say &quot;Yes professor&quot; and &quot;Of course, you're the scientist&quot; and be on your way. And you better get out of the way before the airship battle starts. If you die in their combat, it's your fault.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worse than that. Honestly.<br /> <br /> As much as a love the Etherites, their ethos applied to society would essentially lead to thousands of factions with their own 'scientific theories' who are ready and willing to commit violence on those who trespass on those theories for the honor of their school of thought.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039168#post1039168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To increase the number of people who can be exploited by the West. With lower populations and higher incomes, the developing world would have been less vulnerable to the corporate exploitation that leads to environmental degradation and labor abuses. They do not want to improve the Masses, they just want to exploit the Masses, and they are willing to destroy or kill anything that threatens their exploitation of the Masses. Otherwise, we would have publicly known Asteroid/Moon Mines, Orbital Colonies, and Solar Power Satellites (as well as a wealthier, if smaller, population).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why do they need to exploit anyone? The Technocracy does not need you for your labor. Environmental Degradation is not their fault either. They have zero reason to exploit the masses, at least in the way you suggest. Anything that would require massive numbers of manual labor..... they can trivially create people. Just whole-sale drop people off of an assembly line.<br /> <br /> They do these things to <i>eliminate competing realities.</i> Africa and the middle east, in Mage, are literally different realities. The laws of physics work differently in these places, because the peoples beliefs are, to the perspective of the Technocracy, primitive and deviant.<br /> <br /> Seeing as reality deviance has the potential to spawn world ending horrors. They would be entirely justified in simply vaporizing the population of Africa in atomic fire. Instead they mercifully strike down only those opposed to Unity and work to bring the remainder of the population into the fold. Their success is the success of all.<br /> <br /> ISIS, has a noted tendency to destroy the remains of past civilization do they not? So why wouldn't the union support them temporarily? They're doing the Unions work FOR them. Smashing the remnants of deviant ideologies wherever they find them, while leaving their own structures and holy sites out in the open, where the Union can destroy them at their leisure later.<br /> <br /> Your argument is nonsensical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T18:26:13-08:00","id":1039185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039168#post1039168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To increase the number of people who can be exploited by the West. With lower populations and higher incomes, the developing world would have been less vulnerable to the corporate exploitation that leads to environmental degradation and labor abuses. They do not want to improve the Masses, they just want to exploit the Masses, and they are willing to destroy or kill anything that threatens their exploitation of the Masses. Otherwise, we would have publicly known Asteroid/Moon Mines, Orbital Colonies, and Solar Power Satellites (as well as a wealthier, if smaller, population).</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny how no cavemen or tribal people NEVER went to colonize the Moon guided by their benevolent shamans-priests<br /> <br /> Oh yes, I forgot, those shamans didn't think that ordinary people were worth dwelling with the Gods...<br /> <br /> Wait, but Im sure that after the first civilization, other Mages would've sent people there right?<br /> <br /> Nope.<br /> <br /> The Hermetics could bother to send Doissetep to Mars.<br /> <br /> But they couldn't bother to show the wonders of Umbra to dirty peasents.<br /> <br /> The Dreamspeakers, Verbena, Eutanathoi, Messianic Voices, those would make the Umbras their playground.<br /> <br /> But dumb &quot;mundanes&quot; weren't worth of that prize or those higher revelations.<br /> <br /> After all, they aren't choosen/enlightened/elite.<br /> <br /> No Traditon has EVER bothered about showing the small piece of the wonders of Umbra to the masses.<br /> <br /> The Union however, did sent some citizens to space.<br /> <br /> It wasn't a lot of exploration for the masses, sure.<br /> <br /> But it's still a HELL of a lot more than the Traditions EVER did.<br /> <br /> Besides, it's not like the Union doesn't have in their time table the plans for special exploration<br /> <br /> They do.<br /> <br /> But... Space is dangerous. Far far too dangerous. Have you ever seen what lurks over there?<br /> <br /> Sending unprepared citizens to space would only endanger the masses.<br /> <br /> Also, don't forget: its the Union that keeps Earth safe from the things-men-were-not-meant-to-know.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Traditions aren't fighting the grotesque monstruosities of space.<br /> <br /> They are too busy fighting the Union.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the end of the day, all heavy work will fall to the Union. Again. And the Traditions will keep cursing like spoiled children","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T18:37:25-08:00","id":1039191,"title":"","content":"Then why does the Technocracy, which shapes the Consensus of the entire mortal population, allow such things to happen? The Technocracy controls the Western governments that overthrow the democratically elected governments of the developing world, so why would they allow the governments they control to overthrow democratic and progressive governments if they cared one whit about the Masses? The Technocracy controls (or controlled) the dictatorships that allied with the Western governments, so why would not spread the technology to allow for reproductive freedom beyond the elites of the developing countries if they cared one whit about the Masses?<br /> <br /> And the idea of subjective reality does not exist when you are talking about cWoD crossovers, which is the point of this thread, when we are comparing the effectiveness of Changelings and Mages to represent the ideals of Science Fiction. Physics does not work differently in the non-West than it does in the West in CtD, VtM, or WtA, just in MtA, which suggests that it is the nature of Mages that interferes with technology that they think should not exist rather than the nature of Reality, at least when you are talking about a crossover. In fact, the idea that science or technology would work differently in different locations is completely antithetical to the ideas of Science Fiction, which means that CtD, VtM, and WtA are closer to the ideals of Science Fiction than MtA, which suggests that MtA is really not appropriate for Science Fiction. However, the idea that science and technology is suppressed by 'primitive' beliefs is a great excuse for the Technocracy to justify its genocidal atrocities, mundane or supernatural, that it is responsible for outside of the West.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T19:15:21-08:00","id":1039212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039191#post1039191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why does the Technocracy, which shapes the Consensus of the entire mortal population, allow such things to happen? The Technocracy controls the Western governments that overthrow the democratically elected governments of the developing world, so why would they allow the governments they control to overthrow democratic and progressive governments if they cared one whit about the Masses? The Technocracy controls (or controlled) the dictatorships that allied with the Western governments, so why would not spread the technology to allow for reproductive freedom beyond the elites of the developing countries if they cared one whit about the Masses?<br /> <br /> And the idea of subjective reality does not exist when you are talking about cWoD crossovers, which is the point of this thread, when we are comparing the effectiveness of Changelings and Mages to represent the ideals of Science Fiction. Physics does not work differently in the non-West than it does in the West in CtD, VtM, or WtA, just in MtA, which suggests that it is the nature of Mages that interferes with technology that they think should not exist rather than the nature of Reality, at least when you are talking about a crossover. In fact, the idea that science or technology would work differently in different locations is completely antithetical to the ideas of Science Fiction, which means that CtD, VtM, and WtA are closer to the ideals of Science Fiction than MtA, which suggests that MtA is really not appropriate for Science Fiction. However, the idea that science and technology is suppressed by 'primitive' beliefs is a great excuse for the Technocracy to justify its genocidal atrocities, mundane or supernatural, that it is responsible for outside of the West.</div> </div> </div> </div>It exists so long as mages exist. If you have mages in your setting, as written, then you have a subjective reality. In fact, taking mages version of reality makes MORE sense than trying to come up with any other amalgamation of the other settings. Because Mage, as a setting, can better explain CtD, VtM, or WtA all existing in the same world than ANY of the others can.<br /> <br /> Science and technology is not 'suppressed' by primitive beliefs. Primitive beliefs spawn ten story tall flaming demons that obliterate towns. The technocracy is against ten story tall flaming demons, and so they cut them off at the source.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the technocracy DOES NOT shape the consensus of the entire mortal population alone. The Traditions have their hands in the pot, throwing shit in to try and and screw the technocracy over.<br /> <br /> Camping and wilderness holidays? That's an invention of the Verbena. Carsickness, an invention of, IIRC the Hermetics. Every downside to what the technocracy has given people is the result of well executed interference.<br /> <br /> Because the masses in those countries, are not theirs to care for. They are a bunch of quite literal savages with their heads full of ten thousand years of whatever they thought BEFORE the technocrats came before the Technocracy can make things better, they have to ensure they aren't arming an enemy by wiping out deviancy in their culture.<br /> <br /> And no, Science fiction is full of bullshit like that. &quot;This thing here doesn't work there because thingymajigs.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T20:56:24-08:00","id":1039243,"title":"","content":"Changelling THE DREAMING is not subjective?<br /> <br /> Thats the most banal thing I ever heard...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T22:06:11-08:00","id":1039259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039243#post1039243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelling THE DREAMING is not subjective?<br /> <br /> Thats the most banal thing I ever heard...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not nearly so subjective as Mage is. But it is the exception rather than the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T11:28:45-08:00","id":1039527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039178#post1039178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's worse than that. Honestly.<br /> <br /> As much as a love the Etherites, their ethos applied to society would essentially lead to thousands of factions with their own 'scientific theories' who are ready and willing to commit violence on those who trespass on those theories for the honor of their school of thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically the setting of <a href=\"http://www.girlgeniusonline.com/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Girl Genius</a>.<br /> <br /> A place where Etherite-style mad science rose to prominence instead of the empirical (Technocrat) style we have in our world. Consequently, &quot;Europa&quot; is a chaotic hotbed of intrigue and conflict. Where Science Barons wage war with each other over slights (real or imagined), using armies of clockwork soldiers, zeppelins, ray guns, hoards of bio-engineered super-soldiers, and dangerous weapons of mass destruction. Where the non-mad masses huddle in walled fortresses, afraid of wandering a blasted countryside littered with discarded engines of war, and infested with genetically created bio-weapons and the mindless thralls of brain-jacking machine wasps.<br /> <br /> It's not surprising that one of the most powerful &quot;Sparks&quot; is Baron Wulfenbach, a man who realized that the only way that the world would achieve some level of stability would be if someone conquered the continent and imposed order. And since no one else was competent enough to do it, he did it himself. <a href=\"http://www.girlgeniusonline.com/comic.php?date=20040806#.WIzwzRsrLIU\" target=\"_blank\">And it worked</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T11:39:45-08:00","id":1039530,"title":"","content":"I think the fundamental point is that people are terrible at thinking outside their own perspective, so when in a position of power, they will assume everyone is living in similar circumstances to themselves. When these people in power happen to be Consensus changers, their interpretation becomes so literal that no one else can escape their rule.<br /> <br /> This is what has happened with the Order of Reason, but it wouldn't be any kinder if any other tradition took over.<br /> And yet, the alternative of chaos is exactly how the Nephandi would prefer it.<br /> <br /> We have arrived at Rock, and shall be proceeding to Hard Place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T11:58:06-08:00","id":1039539,"title":"","content":"Well what happened to the Order of Reason as of current metaplot state is that they got taken over by the evil aliens. Which is an extremely dull and uninspired way to give a white hat to the Technocrats if you ask me. &quot;Oh, your leadership has been Cylons all along but now you, Johnny Technocrat, can join the good fight against them!&quot; Bleh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 01-28-2017, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T12:03:15-08:00","id":1039540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039539#post1039539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well what happened to the Order of Reason as of current metaplot state is that they got taken over by the evil aliens. Which is an extremely dull and uninspired way to give a white hat to the Technocrats if you ask me. &amp;quot;Oh, your leadership has been Cylons all along, but now you, Johnny Technocrat can join the good fight against them!&amp;quot; Bleh.</div> </div> </div> </div>R...r...really?<br /> <br /> Oh boy... That's... Disapointing...<br /> <br /> And I liked that scenario of &quot;Etherite Victory&quot;. I'll make some dystopian nightmares in the Umbra to represent the &quot;Utopy&quot; of each one of the Traditions, that would be awsome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T12:06:26-08:00","id":1039542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039540#post1039540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> R...r...really?<br /> <br /> Oh boy... That's... Disapointing...<br /> <br /> And I liked that scenario of &quot;Etherite Victory&quot;. I'll make some dystopian nightmares in the Umbra to represent the &quot;Utopy&quot; of each one of the Traditions, that would be awsome</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Check out the Revised Convention books, Void Engineers specifically. I like them overall, but the plot bits let me down. The Technocratic leadership was stranded in Deep Umbra during the avatar storm and got transformed into evil aliens leading evil versions of the Conventions. &quot;Threat Null&quot; they are called. I assume that blacker suits and evil eye liner were part of the deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T12:10:00-08:00","id":1039543,"title":"","content":"It is just the nature of Transhumanity. When you remove what is human, what is left? You end up with monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T12:18:05-08:00","id":1039546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039542#post1039542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. Check out the Revised Convention books, Void Engineers specifically. I like them overall, but the plot bits let me down. The Technocratic leadership was stranded in Deep Umbra during the avatar storm and got transformed into evil aliens leading evil versions of the Conventions. &quot;Threat Null&quot; they are called. I assume that blacker suits and evil eye liner were part of the deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Control hasn't been leading the technocrats since the Dimensional Anomaly. Since then they've been managing themselves. Threat Null is what happened after Control was cut off for good. As it stands, Threat Null have no real influence on the Technocracy as a whole, outside of convincing others to join their cause.<br /> <br /> Also, except from high ranking personel in the VE, pretty much no one is aware Threat Null exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-30-2017, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T12:20:58-08:00","id":1039547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039543#post1039543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is just the nature of Transhumanity. When you remove what is human, what is left? You end up with monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Implying that there is a standard definition of what is human.<br /> <br /> Also, if you hate transhumanism so much then I sure hope you are not relying on any medicine to help you to survive. Because using medicine to overcome limits of human body is part of transhumanism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T12:47:13-08:00","id":1039564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039543#post1039543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is just the nature of Transhumanity. When you remove what is human, what is left? You end up with monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like those monstruous Verbena shapeshifters? Or those inhuman Dreamspeakers always housing alien spirits inside their bodies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T13:13:32-08:00","id":1039575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039543#post1039543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is just the nature of Transhumanity. When you remove what is human, what is left? You end up with monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>So lemme ask you this. Do your Mage characters run around and destroy prosthetic limb clinics? Is a guy with a pacemaker an enemy that needs to be fireballed on sight? Do they knock eyeglasses off the eyes of school children and kick Stephen Hawking out of his wheelchair?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T13:25:16-08:00","id":1039578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039575#post1039575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So lemme ask you this. Do your Mage characters run around and destroy prosthetic limb clinics? Is a guy with a pacemaker an enemy that needs to be fireballed on sight? Do they knock eyeglasses off the eyes of school children and kick Stephen Hawking out of his wheelchair?</div> </div> </div> </div>The man is clearly a cybernetic Antichrist set up by the Technocracy to undermine humanity with the lies of science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T14:14:17-08:00","id":1039594,"title":"","content":"This is such a interesting idea for a static marauder. A guy who sees all these things as examples of transgumanism and must be destroyed in order to avoid mankinds downfall to the machine","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T15:32:36-08:00","id":1039631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1039594#post1039594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is such a interesting idea for a static marauder. A guy who sees all these things as examples of transgumanism and must be destroyed in order to avoid mankinds downfall to the machine</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be a very short living interesting character.<br /> <br /> Well, that's almost the description of Marauders...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T19:45:15-08:00","id":1039761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last time I checked, the ideal of the old Hermetics was that only the worthy can have the power and rights, and that only Hermetics are worthy. The founding of the Order of Hermes in the 9th century wasn't followed by the Renaissance - that was five hundred years later.</div> </div> </div> </div>As per DA Mage, The Craftmasons were a small band of rogue Hermetics that were around at the Dark Ages, centuries before the Renaissance. In some ways, it can be argued that they created the Renaissance.<br /> <br /> Having said that, let's talk of what it's &quot;to be worthy&quot; for a Hermetic. It doesn't mean to have been chosed by god/ the gods/ the spirits. It doesn't mean to have been born of a mystic bloodline (albeit that can help). It's obvious that it means to have Hermetic Magick(tm), but since being able to do magic means different things to different mages, it's important to understand what's magick, to understand what are &quot;the worthy&quot;.<br /> <br /> To resume what the books say about this, for the Hermetics, all the humans, as beings created at image of God, share His authority over the creation. That's the general Why of Magick. But you can't just be a human and have all of this, no. You need to work hard, study, prepare, to get to command Creation.<br /> Incidentally, this it's the manifest destiny of humanity as per the Trad. Book. Everyone should be able to throw thunders. In other words, if you aren't a Mage it's not because your destiny or choice, but because you are lazy, idiot, or just mediocre.<br /> <br /> This are the &quot;worthy&quot;, the elite that has done their homework, and thus sits at the top of the pyramid.<br /> In the good side, this means that they have reasons to teach what they know (it's law to get an apprentice if you want to advance in the Order). In the bad side, this means that they don't have time for the low witted, if you don't have talent, go fuck yourself.<br /> <br /> But let's start from the begining. This idea of &quot;Human as inheritors of the power and authority of God&quot; it's always present. It put's humanity at a very central place in the cosmology. It's not just that god loves humans the most, but rather than he gave humans the keys to run the Creation at fucking Will. This it's the pedestal that I talked before.<br /> Non mage humans aren't shit because Humanity isn't important, but rather because they are seen as morons that haven't lived up to that high place.<br /> <br /> This foundation it's, too, in the Craftmason ideal, but with a twist. For the Craftmason, the normal people isn't less capable of ruling and shaping the world, they're just slower.<br /> Craftmasons took the idea that Humanity can rule the creation, but stated that you don't need to be a Mage to do that. Magick makes things easier, but it's a tool, not an end. A tool that can be shared.<br /> <br /> If wasn't for how uppity was the Order of Hermes, refusing to help &quot;the lowly peasants&quot;, the Craftmasosn could have been a House more, but in the end, the idea that non mage humans are as important as human mages was too much of a break of the Hermetic Paradigm, and they had to leave.<br /> Incidentaly, this was also what caused their extermination at the hands of the Technocracy they helped to build. Most Technocrats wanted to control what the masses were allowed to have, Craftmasons believed that the masses, not being inferior in any way, deserved every bit as much as Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-28-2017, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:05:45-08:00","id":1039773,"title":"","content":"Which is one of the first tragedies of the Technocracy. If the Craftmasons had maintained their position and influence in the Technocracy, the benefits of science and technology would have likely been spread more equally among the Masses, allowing for even greater advances in science and technology, and there would likely by a human civilization spread throughout the Inner Sol System. In addition, I think that the relationship between the Technocracy and the Traditions would have been much more cordial, a competition rather than a war, and the Nephandi would be having a really hard time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:29:40-08:00","id":1040138,"title":"","content":"I honestly can't tell if you guys are seriously trying to argue with each other or trying to reenact the most stereotypical Traditions vs Technocracy online argument ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:33:58-08:00","id":1040142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1040138#post1040138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly can't tell if you guys are seriously trying to argue with each other or trying to reenact the most stereotypical Traditions vs Technocracy online argument ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is what things are like when you stick them in a room together, then I can sympathise with the nephandi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T20:49:47-08:00","id":1040396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1040142#post1040142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If this is what things are like when you stick them in a room together, then I can sympathise with the nephandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would an enlightened agent waste time trying to put some sense on a traditionalist's head? Just zap them and be done with it. If weren't for that Turing traitor, we wouldn't need that discussion.<br /> <br /> Luckly, we have the perfect tool to make them understand. Room 101.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:39:25-08:00","id":1041526,"title":"","content":"Well, mystical Traditionalists can call on their Changeling allies and laugh as the Technocrats start gibbering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T18:46:29-08:00","id":1041624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041526#post1041526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, mystical Traditionalists can call on their Changeling allies and laugh as the Technocrats start gibbering.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the changeling allies who literally fall sick and die just from being in the presence of a technocrat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T19:11:16-08:00","id":1041631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041624#post1041624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean the changeling allies who literally fall sick and die just from being in the presence of a technocrat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechnically speaking, it does neither, as it increases temporary Banality by a bit. Changelings that had high temp Banality already would be temporarily undone and revert to being human, while those who are not so encumbered can still call upon the Wyrd and such. The only beings that die of this are those who, like the mer, end up turning into normal humans in places where normal humans cannot survive. Also, the merdhuacha seemed to have an easier time with it, at least in the fiction, since a mated pair of them killed a VE EFD exploratory team, with the distaff side of the pair laying her eggs in their drowned corpses.<br /> <br /> C20 is probably going to make changelings way more resilient in this regard. At the very least, the prospect of unleashing Arts means that the &quot;technocratic badass&quot; suddenly has to worry about everything around him or her being on fire, space and locality being disrupted, however it ends up working. Be prepared to be the butt of your amalgam's jokes for years if one unleashes Kryos and/or Skycraft.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, sorry about that. I guess when it comes to how you were encased in a block of ice, we should really just <i>let it go</i>.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T19:22:06-08:00","id":1041640,"title":"","content":"No Changeling will fall sick or die near a Technocrat (weak Chimera will start taking damage if they are in close proximity to a creature with high Banality though). Changelings gain one point of temporary Banality per full scene that they spend in the presence of an entity with a Banality above 7 (Changeling, p. 153). Since Changelings will be trying to shatter the mind of a Technocrat instead of having a drink with a Technocrat, I doubt they will have much to worry about.<br /> <br /> Changelings can invoke the Dreaming by Calling the Wyrd, allowing their Faerie Mien and all of their Chimera to be seen by everyone in view, so Technocrats only need to be in line of sight of Changelings to bug out and God help a Technocrat who is Enchanted before being killed by chimerical damage. At best, they remember only a faint dream of the events and, if killed by chimerical damage, are in a coma for a month. At worst, they have no memory of the events and, if killed by chimerical damage, are in a coma for a year.<br /> <br /> The Mists will hide the Changelings (and their companions) from the memory of the Technocrats as soon as they are out of view. Recording technology will fail as the Mists erase footage and sound and even written descriptions will fade within a couple of days (typed lines on a computer will likely fade whenever the attention of the typist moves). If Changelings are willing to risk the temporary Banality, they could walk right into a Technocratic facility after Calling the Wyrd and take whatever they wanted. The Technocrats would turn to get help, forget what they were doing, and be stuck in that loop until the Changeling left the area.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T19:47:50-08:00","id":1041645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041631#post1041631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mechnically speaking, it does neither, as it increases temporary Banality by a bit. Changelings that had high temp Banality already would be temporarily undone and revert to being human, while those who are not so encumbered can still call upon the Wyrd and such. The only beings that die of this are those who, like the mer, end up turning into normal humans in places where normal humans cannot survive. Also, the merdhuacha seemed to have an easier time with it, at least in the fiction, since a mated pair of them killed a VE EFD exploratory team, with the distaff side of the pair laying her eggs in their drowned corpses.<br /> <br /> C20 is probably going to make changelings way more resilient in this regard. At the very least, the prospect of unleashing Arts means that the &quot;technocratic badass&quot; suddenly has to worry about everything around him or her being on fire, space and locality being disrupted, however it ends up working. Be prepared to be the butt of your amalgam's jokes for years if one unleashes Kryos and/or Skycraft.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, sorry about that. I guess when it comes to how you were encased in a block of ice, we should really just <i>let it go</i>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The VE are also the lowest banality of the conventions. But I was given to understand that banality at 8+ caused actual physical harm to the changeling in question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T20:02:21-08:00","id":1041652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041640#post1041640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Changeling will fall sick or die near a Technocrat (weak Chimera will start taking damage if they are in close proximity to a creature with high Banality though). Changelings gain one point of temporary Banality per full scene that they spend in the presence of an entity with a Banality above 7 (Changeling, p. 153). Since Changelings will be trying to shatter the mind of a Technocrat instead of having a drink with a Technocrat, I doubt they will have much to worry about.<br /> <br /> Changelings can invoke the Dreaming by Calling the Wyrd, allowing their Faerie Mien and all of their Chimera to be seen by everyone in view, so Technocrats only need to be in line of sight of Changelings to bug out and God help a Technocrat who is Enchanted before being killed by chimerical damage. At best, they remember only a faint dream of the events and, if killed by chimerical damage, are in a coma for a month. At worst, they have no memory of the events and, if killed by chimerical damage, are in a coma for a year.<br /> <br /> The Mists will hide the Changelings (and their companions) from the memory of the Technocrats as soon as they are out of view. Recording technology will fail as the Mists erase footage and sound and even written descriptions will fade within a couple of days (typed lines on a computer will likely fade whenever the attention of the typist moves). If Changelings are willing to risk the temporary Banality, they could walk right into a Technocratic facility after Calling the Wyrd and take whatever they wanted. The Technocrats would turn to get help, forget what they were doing, and be stuck in that loop until the Changeling left the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>You literally cannot enchant a technocrat. VE aside.<br /> <br /> It simply can't be done as it would require a technocrat to play along and accept it. Which they literally cannot do thanks to mental conditioning. Just like a technocrat can't allow a hermetic to cast buffs on or heal them with 'magic'. willingly.<br /> <br /> The mists effect mortals. Technocrats, even those who ARE mortals, don't count as mortals. Also thanks to mental conditioning. This is why Joe the non-mage can take a plasma cannon and melt faces with it without the whole thing exploding in paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T20:03:55-08:00","id":1041653,"title":"","content":"Nope, not at all, it just causes them to gain temporary points of Banality at an accelerated rate ([Individual's Banality] - 7 points per scene of association), so they prefer to stay away from such people and avoid associating with them as they would a leper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T20:04:38-08:00","id":1041654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041645#post1041645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The VE are also the lowest banality of the conventions. But I was given to understand that banality at 8+ caused actual physical harm to the changeling in question?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was only for one of the Kiths, like the Sidhe. Not certain though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T20:16:45-08:00","id":1041658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041652#post1041652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You literally cannot enchant a technocrat. VE aside.<br /> <br /> It simply can't be done as it would require a technocrat to play along and accept it. Which they literally cannot do thanks to mental conditioning. Just like a technocrat can't allow a hermetic to cast buffs on or heal them with 'magic'. willingly.<br /> <br /> The mists effect mortals. Technocrats, even those who ARE mortals, don't count as mortals. Also thanks to mental conditioning. This is why Joe the non-mage can take a plasma cannon and melt faces with it without the whole thing exploding in paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, Technocrats are considered to be Unenchanted supernaturals and the Mists effect Unenchanted supernaturals as much as they effect Unenchanted mortals (Changeling, p. 208). The Dreaming is more powerful than any Mage, even the Oracles, who know better than the mess around with the Dreaming (Dreams and Nightmares, p. 44). The Technocracy is the least capable entity for dealing with Changelings and the Dreaming, consult your local Verbena instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T20:29:19-08:00","id":1041665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041645#post1041645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The VE are also the lowest banality of the conventions. But I was given to understand that banality at 8+ caused actual physical harm to the changeling in question?</div> </div> </div> </div>And the merdhuacha are inveterate* ravagers who rely on having a fairly high Banality to rip Glamour from out of the fear of their victims, so they're pretty well proof against the system that Aya Tari mentioned.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*And invertebrate!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:23:06-08:00","id":1041813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041658#post1041658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, Technocrats are considered to be Unenchanted supernaturals and the Mists effect Unenchanted supernaturals as much as they effect Unenchanted mortals (Changeling, p. 208). The Dreaming is more powerful than any Mage, even the Oracles, who know better than the mess around with the Dreaming (Dreams and Nightmares, p. 44). The Technocracy is the least capable entity for dealing with Changelings and the Dreaming, consult your local Verbena instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>The dreaming is a mental realm. It's not some entity, and two, the Technocracy can deal with changelings and the dreaming as easily as they deal with anything else. with prime 2, bullets hit chimerical beings just as well as they do anything else. With Mind 3, they can cleanse the area of glamour by re-angling the places innate resonance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:42:11-08:00","id":1041846,"title":"","content":"Do you have book and page number to back up your statements with canon game mechanics? Because I have provided mine already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:22:12-08:00","id":1041869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041846#post1041846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have book and page number to back up your statements with canon game mechanics? Because I have provided mine already.</div> </div> </div> </div>A book about changeling hardly has to do with Mage. I wouldn't pay any attention to what changeling has to says about Mages than I would to how Mages view vampires.<br /> <br /> Vampires are, contrary to what the technocracy believes, not blood cults of mages.<br /> <br /> Just as how Humans are not creatures of the Weaver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 02-01-2017, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:34:53-08:00","id":1041872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041869#post1041869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A book about changeling hardly has to do with Mage. I wouldn't pay any attention to what changeling has to says about Mages than I would to how Mages view vampires.<br /> <br /> Vampires are, contrary to what the technocracy believes, not blood cults of mages.<br /> <br /> Just as how Humans are not creatures of the Weaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... does that mean you made the stuff you said up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:34:54-08:00","id":1041873,"title":"","content":"When we look at the books that deal with the Mists and the Dreaming, there are specific rules on how Mages, Vampires, Werewolves, etc deal with the Mists and the Dreaming. Now, if there are specific crossover rules in Mage that contradict the rules in Changeling, please share them by giving a specific book and a specific page. If there are no contradictory crossover rules though, the Changeling rules are canon and trump any headcannon you may have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:44:27-08:00","id":1041881,"title":"","content":"No, it is fair to say the game lines are separate and that changeling rules for handling mages don't necessarily apply unless you are running an actual crossover. Edit: and then it depends on what kind of crossover.<br /> <br /> Input from other games is informative, but it isn't binding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 02-01-2017, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:47:52-08:00","id":1041884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041872#post1041872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... does that mean you made the stuff you said up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially. They're logical extrapolations of the rules of mage. Glamour is tass with a particular resonance. As is Vitae and Gnosis. By changing that resonance, it is no longer Glamour but simply Tass. Alternatively, one could CREATE glamour if they knew what resonance to give the quintessence when creating tass and had the ability to.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 makes weapons that extend into other realms of existence, as the dreaming is one such realm....<br /> <br /> I do not recall where I've seen mention of the dreaming before, however I have seen it. It's a realm. The MISTS are an entity, however like any entity they can be countered with sufficient application of magic. In this case a simple mental defense or mental backup.<br /> <br /> Like every single member of Iteration X has. and some other conventions besides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:16:07-08:00","id":1041896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041884#post1041884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Essentially. They're logical extrapolations of the rules of mage. Glamour is tass with a particular resonance. As is Vitae and Gnosis. By changing that resonance, it is no longer Glamour but simply Tass. Alternatively, one could CREATE glamour if they knew what resonance to give the quintessence when creating tass and had the ability to.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 makes weapons that extend into other realms of existence, as the dreaming is one such realm....<br /> <br /> I do not recall where I've seen mention of the dreaming before, however I have seen it. It's a realm. The MISTS are an entity, however like any entity they can be countered with sufficient application of magic. In this case a simple mental defense or mental backup.<br /> <br /> Like every single member of Iteration X has. and some other conventions besides.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you aren't citing specific authorial mentions, you might not want to make casually definitive pronouncements about what Mages can and cannot do versus other game lines. <br /> <br /> Here's a catch twenty two. You have these Prime bullets that can hit Chimera. How do you see the Chimera to hit them though? The only way for non-Changelings to perceive Chimera is to be Enchanted. You earlier said that Technocrats cannot become Enchanted (which I don't agree with but let's take it at face value). How do you hit the thing you cannot perceive without being Enchanted if you cannot be Enchanted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:17:29-08:00","id":1041897,"title":"","content":"Alright, just so we are clear, Enginseer-42 is saying that their positions are just headcannon and that there are no canon rules that support their position in either Changeling or Mage. Just to clarify, the Dreaming is an entity with countless Realms and the Mists are its defenses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-01-2017, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:18:59-08:00","id":1041900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041884#post1041884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Essentially. They're logical extrapolations of the rules of mage. Glamour is tass with a particular resonance. As is Vitae and Gnosis. By changing that resonance, it is no longer Glamour but simply Tass. Alternatively, one could CREATE glamour if they knew what resonance to give the quintessence when creating tass and had the ability to.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 makes weapons that extend into other realms of existence, as the dreaming is one such realm....<br /> <br /> I do not recall where I've seen mention of the dreaming before, however I have seen it. It's a realm. The MISTS are an entity, however like any entity they can be countered with sufficient application of magic. In this case a simple mental defense or mental backup.<br /> <br /> Like every single member of Iteration X has. and some other conventions besides.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure changing the resonance of Glamour would stop it being Glamour. Glamour itself could have all kinds of resonance depending on who was using it. It's like how the Gnosis can have different kinds of resonance depending on what the Garou has been through. Wyrm Taint being a particularly strong and volatile one.<br /> <br /> But Wyrm tainted Gnosis is still Gnosis. The resonance doesn't stop it being so.<br /> <br /> See, I go with the idea that Glamour, Gnosis, Vitae, and Pathos, all of this to the mage is just Quintessence under different names. The TASS is just how it's stored, so Blood for the Vamps, and Ectoplasm for both the Wraiths and the Werewolves. But essentially it's all Quintessence.<br /> <br /> &quot;Creating&quot; Glamour should be as simple as having quintessence to give them. The Verbena Book even talks about a small coven of Verbena who try to feed a starving Chimeric creature some of their own quintessence to restore its glamour.<br /> <br /> The only thing about taking Quint from other Supernaturals is you'll need more than Prime to do it. Vamps need Prime, Life and Matter. Werewolves would need Prime and Spirit (and maybe Life). Wraiths could be just Prime and Spirit (though you could argue you'd need Entropy as well, especially if they were a Spectre). while Fae would need Prime and Mind (and possibly Spirit).<br /> <br /> I think it's intentionally designed for sucking away Quint from other Supernats to be a fairly difficult thing to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 02-01-2017, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:29:13-08:00","id":1041903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041897#post1041897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just to clarify, the Dreaming is an entity with countless Realms and the Mists are its defenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... actually no more true than what Enginseer has been saying. Sorry. The Dreaming is a place (in as much as the Umbra or the Shadowlands are &quot;places&quot;). There are people in the setting who believe that the Dreaming is alive and has a will of its own, but that's not an explicit canonical truth. The Mists are also not an attack dog that erases the memories of people who interact with Changeling-stuff. Its a side effect, like Delirium. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:30:00-08:00","id":1041905,"title":"","content":"No, Spirit is required to interact with entities of the Dreaming (the Dreaming is a spiritual Universe, not a mental Realm). It specifically says so on p. 22 of the Book of Lost Dreams. Which is another reason why most members of the Technocrats are woefully outmatched by the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:31:50-08:00","id":1041906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041905#post1041905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Spirit is required to interact with entities of the Dreaming (the Dreaming is a spiritual Universe, not a mental Realm). It specifically says so on p. 22 of the Book of Lost Dreams. Which is another reason why most members of the Technocrats are woefully outmatched by the Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not understanding how that contradicts what I said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:37:56-08:00","id":1041910,"title":"","content":"Look at Dreams and Nightmares p. 31, 'Mages would do well to understand that the Dreaming takes care of Itself and Its minions. The Dreaming is alive, though not in any way that mere mortals can understand'. The Dreaming is a living entity, after a fashion, and consciously attacks and destroys anything that endangers It or Its minions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:53:53-08:00","id":1041921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041910#post1041910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at Dreams and Nightmares p. 31, 'Mages would do well to understand that the Dreaming takes care of Itself and Its minions. The Dreaming is alive, though not in any way that mere mortals can understand'. The Dreaming is a living entity, after a fashion, and consciously attacks and destroys anything that endangers It or Its minions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The important riders on that are &quot;not in a way that mere mortals can understand&quot; and &quot;after a fashion.&quot; Conscious agency is something that you're reading into it. Which is admittedly something that many Changelings do in the setting as well. I'm not saying the Dreaming is definitively <i>not</i> alive, just that its an open question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T12:49:16-08:00","id":1041968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041897#post1041897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, just so we are clear, Enginseer-42 is saying that their positions are just headcannon and that there are no canon rules that support their position in either Changeling or Mage. Just to clarify, the Dreaming is an entity with countless Realms and the Mists are its defenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of canon rules to support it, they just don't explicitly state it. That's the way mage works. Unlike other splats it doesn't TRY to define every possible instance of things interacting, because even the included rules are at best guidelines to magic. Ease of use things. It's intended for the storyteller to work out HOW these things work in each situation themselves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:04:34-08:00","id":1041982,"title":"","content":"&quot;Rules that don't explicitly state&quot; is another way to say &quot;This is how I interpret them&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, Mage dos lead to ST interpretation for a smooth running, but that doesn't valid yours as the Univeral truth only as your paradigm (sorry couldn't help it, don't hit me!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> There is clearly a difference of interpretaion on what the Dreaming &amp; the Mist is, which I'm not gonna pour more oil on, because it's thr Mage sub forum &amp; I'm on the Changeling side (and I usually dislike Mage point of view on othe splats).<br /> <br /> I'm just gonna raise another crossover rule that I'm surprised wasn't mentioned, about the Changeling using their own banality to counter Mages Magick. Would make any Technocrat nothing more than a human with weird tech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:12:58-08:00","id":1041986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041982#post1041982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Rules that don't explicitly state&quot; is another way to say &quot;This is how I interpret them&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, Mage dos lead to ST interpretation for a smooth running, but that doesn't valid yours as the Univeral truth only as your paradigm (sorry couldn't help it, don't hit me!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> There is clearly a difference of interpretaion on what the Dreaming &amp; the Mist is, which I'm not gonna pour more oil on, because it's thr Mage sub forum &amp; I'm on the Changeling side (and I usually dislike Mage point of view on othe splats).</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's one thing the Mage books do pretty well, its the way they convey just how arrogant mages really are. They are humanities next step and my goodness don't they know it. This bleeds in to all their interactions with other supernatural creatures, and how they think that, because they're mages and thus are theoretically capable of seeing everything and meeting everyone, that also means that collectively they know everything about everyone else.<br /> <br /> The Mage point of view on these guys is basically this; the mage looking at a werewolf and going &quot;ah yes, a garou, one of the servants of an ancient spirit known as Gaia, one of the many spiritual gods there are. You needn't fight so hard, I've read of thousands of spirits like your Gaia, I'm sure you can get another one.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:13:05-08:00","id":1041987,"title":"","content":"When it comes to a conflict between explicitly stated rules and the interpretation of another gamer in our discussions, I tend to go with the explicitly stated rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:14:41-08:00","id":1041988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041987#post1041987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to a conflict between explicitly stated rules and the interpretation of another gamer in our discussions, I tend to go with the explicitly stated rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the interpretation makes more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:37:37-08:00","id":1042038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041982#post1041982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Rules that don't explicitly state&quot; is another way to say &quot;This is how I interpret them&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, Mage dos lead to ST interpretation for a smooth running, but that doesn't valid yours as the Univeral truth only as your paradigm (sorry couldn't help it, don't hit me!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> There is clearly a difference of interpretaion on what the Dreaming &amp; the Mist is, which I'm not gonna pour more oil on, because it's thr Mage sub forum &amp; I'm on the Changeling side (and I usually dislike Mage point of view on othe splats).<br /> <br /> I'm just gonna raise another crossover rule that I'm surprised wasn't mentioned, about the Changeling using their own banality to counter Mages Magick. Would make any Technocrat nothing more than a human with weird tech.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! And I'm sure there are plenty of mages who's paradigms hold that the dreaming is an unstoppable godlike force and thus can do jack and shit against it.<br /> <br /> Then you get the ones who don't. And are merely ignorant of it. Who are effected as normal but could potentially do something against it if they realized what was going on.<br /> <br /> Then you get the ones who are massive bastards and not only know it exists, but view it as firmly beneath them. Though these are rare.<br /> <br /> Changelings can unweave spells, but they'd have to realize it was a spell first, and since they gain banality EVERY SINGLE TIME they do it, they'd be shooting themselves in the foot since the technocrats can just keep firing the laser guns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1041986#post1041986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's one thing the Mage books do pretty well, its the way they convey just how arrogant mages really are. They are humanities next step and my goodness don't they know it. This bleeds in to all their interactions with other supernatural creatures, and how they think that, because they're mages and thus are theoretically capable of seeing everything and meeting everyone, that also means that collectively they know everything about everyone else.<br /> <br /> The Mage point of view on these guys is basically this; the mage looking at a werewolf and going &quot;ah yes, a garou, one of the servants of an ancient spirit known as Gaia, one of the many spiritual gods there are. You needn't fight so hard, I've read of thousands of spirits like your Gaia, I'm sure you can get another one.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, this is totally true and valid. There is a crossover game I'm part of, one of the changelings 'opinion' quote for Mages in general is &quot;Expecto Patronizing.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 02-01-2017, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:45:07-08:00","id":1042044,"title":"","content":"But the Dreaming itself dissolves True Magick like acid because it can unravel Patterns. I am sort of confused why there is the insistence that there is nothing the Technocrats cannot beat. Every other supernatural factions faces unconquerable foes (the Antediluvians for the Kindred, the Wyrm for the Garou, etc). Why not just accept that the Dreaming is the natural and unconquerable antithesis to the Technocracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:48:03-08:00","id":1042045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042038#post1042038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changelings can unweave spells, but they'd have to realize it was a spell first, and since they gain banality EVERY SINGLE TIME they do it, they'd be shooting themselves in the foot since the technocrats can just keep firing the laser guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also not strictly true. Changelings can specifically counteract Changeling Arts in this way. Whether or not they can apply the same effect to True Magick and whether it would still give them Banality to do so is entirely in the realm of speculation and house ruling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:49:43-08:00","id":1042048,"title":"","content":"It's not directly permanent dots of banality, since a Mage without spell is basically a human, a Changeling should be able to dispatch it before gaining a permanent dot of banality.<br /> <br /> And then just go on a wonderful quest in the Dreaming to wash away that pesky banality (and anyway a permanent dot is still probably better than what the Technocrat was planning to do).<br /> <br /> There is just 2 things I'd like to point (of which I'm not sure because I'm not deeply familiar with Mage rules):<br /> -First I thought Mage's paradigm had no impact on the Umbra and it's rules/reality/etc, if that's so, there is no reason for the paradigm to affect the Dreaming either<br /> -Second, in the same way, I was under the impression that a paradigm didn't affect the ability of other splat, for example not believing in Vampire is not gonna stop the Vampire in front of you to do all is bloody tricks, so a Technocrat not believing in Fae doesn't protect him from the Mist, enchantement &amp; such<br /> <br /> But honestly that would be nice, if Onyx PAth could get a real crososver book (for rules only, people will never agree on fluff/meta/stuff anyway)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:50:26-08:00","id":1042050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042044#post1042044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Dreaming itself dissolves True Magick like acid because it can unravel Patterns. I am sort of confused why there is the insistence that there is nothing the Technocrats cannot beat. Every other supernatural factions faces unconquerable foes (the Antediluvians for the Kindred, the Wyrm for the Garou, etc). Why not just accept that the Dreaming is the natural and unconquerable antithesis to the Technocracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because &quot;why not just accept&quot; doesn't really fly in the Mage forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:04:50-08:00","id":1042058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042044#post1042044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Dreaming itself dissolves True Magick like acid because it can unravel Patterns. I am sort of confused why there is the insistence that there is nothing the Technocrats cannot beat. Every other supernatural factions faces unconquerable foes (the Antediluvians for the Kindred, the Wyrm for the Garou, etc). Why not just accept that the Dreaming is the natural and unconquerable antithesis to the Technocracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the simple reason that there is, quite explicitly, nothing that cannot theoretically be done with true magic. Even the limits that we use to play the game are psychological blocks on the part of the player characters, this is HOW magic is generally taught and how it is generally learned. And there are even examples within the rules themselves of things that violate those rules with no real explanation or reason. The flintlock pistol that shoots lightning but causes no paradox and requires no quintessence, for example. Mage is a game about infinite possibilities, and thus infinite mysteries. Nothing is really revealed to you beyond what one set of people BELIEVE about why things happen. How things work.<br /> <br /> The other splats are all about being this badass amongst a world of cardboard, but having some unconquerable foe that even you, in all your might cannot defeat.<br /> <br /> Mage is about being one of those suckers made of cardboard realizing that they CAN do something about their situation. They CAN beat anything and anyone, if they're only good enough. If they're clever enough. If they BELIEVE enough. Do they always succeed? No. They don't. But mage is about being something that fundementally does not follow the same rules as everyone else. Sometimes this puts them on the top of the heap. Other times it drops them to the bottom. Even the technocrats have their highs and lows. Which is why so much of their organization is invested in mortals. To hold the line while the enlightened agents are busy exploding due to the paradox of the latest HITmark.<br /> <br /> Mage is about being a weak frail bastard who refuses to stop because, against what everyone would tell them, there is hope of victory. About taking that hope and forging it into a sword and either going down in a blaze of glory, or bending all of reality to your will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042048#post1042048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not directly permanent dots of banality, since a Mage without spell is basically a human, a Changeling should be able to dispatch it before gaining a permanent dot of banality.<br /> <br /> And then just go on a wonderful quest in the Dreaming to wash away that pesky banality (and anyway a permanent dot is still probably better than what the Technocrat was planning to do).<br /> <br /> There is just 2 things I'd like to point (of which I'm not sure because I'm not deeply familiar with Mage rules):<br /> -First I thought Mage's paradigm had no impact on the Umbra and it's rules/reality/etc, if that's so, there is no reason for the paradigm to affect the Dreaming either<br /> -Second, in the same way, I was under the impression that a paradigm didn't affect the ability of other splat, for example not believing in Vampire is not gonna stop the Vampire in front of you to do all is bloody tricks, so a Technocrat not believing in Fae doesn't protect him from the Mist, enchantement &amp; such<br /> <br /> But honestly that would be nice, if Onyx PAth could get a real crososver book (for rules only, people will never agree on fluff/meta/stuff anyway)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a temporary dot of banality to cancel ONE spell. Then the technocrat fires their gun again and they have to do it again. if they do this every turn until the technocrat runs out of ammo for their laser they will accrue QUITE a hefty bit of banality. 20 points, if the technocrat is at full ammo.<br /> <br /> It would certainly be a problem for the technocrat, but it wouldn't exactly render them impotent either, given they could just pull out a regular gun and use that instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 02-01-2017, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:11:16-08:00","id":1042062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042058#post1042058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would certainly be a problem for the technocrat, but it wouldn't exactly render them impotent either, given they could just pull out a regular gun and use that instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially if these bullets happened to be made of Cold Iron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:24:11-08:00","id":1042072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042058#post1042058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a temporary dot of banality to cancel ONE spell. Then the technocrat fires their gun again and they have to do it again. if they do this every turn until the technocrat runs out of ammo for their laser they will accrue QUITE a hefty bit of banality. 20 points, if the technocrat is at full ammo.<br /> <br /> It would certainly be a problem for the technocrat, but it wouldn't exactly render them impotent either, given they could just pull out a regular gun and use that instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>...because the Changeling is suppose to do nothing else but countering the laser? (which is a reflexive action)<br /> I'm not sure if Mage can counter Arts the same way, but even if they do, a Changeling can still call upon the Wyrd and invoke the Dragon's Ire (all reflexive), and then attack with a big ol'sword<br /> In their Fae Mien, they can soak lethal dammage of a normal gun, I'm not so sure about the Mage (and if you bring Technocrats Exo Armor, we can bring the Nocker's)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042062#post1042062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Especially if these bullets happened to be made of Cold Iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cold Iron while not clearly defined, is definitely barely processed, any bullet made for Modern gun wouldn't fit, you'd have to have a really old gun to have it work (with a risk of it exploding in your hands)<br /> And any magical attempt to create cold iron would fail, because that's what cold iron is.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that Changeling wipe the floor with Mage &amp; Technocrats, but they can definitely defend themselves.<br /> <br /> (and anyway most of this might change greatly with C20)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:28:26-08:00","id":1042075,"title":"","content":"Cold iron is defined as wrought iron, so it is really unsuitable for bullets because you have to cold hammer the bullet into shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:28:44-08:00","id":1042077,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ny24zPeQLks\" target=\"_blank\">Suitable theme for a mage up against impossible odds.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Why would they use cold iron when they could use primium? Aggravated damage against everything, AND countermagics their magic as it passes through? Though how that would work against changelings is kind of unknown.<br /> <br /> Slight advantage to a changelings dispelling abilities, I hadn't realized it was an inherent counterspell. Though now that I've looked up the exact dice mechanics, that renders it a bit... less intimidating. They roll their permanent banality vs the spell itself. Given the technocracies fondness for artifacts, unless they counter ALL successes, unlikely with low banality changelings, the effect still happens. And if they're high enough banality to regularly shut down effects, they're at very strong risk of being undone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 02-01-2017, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:39:18-08:00","id":1042084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042075#post1042075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cold iron is defined as wrought iron, so it is really unsuitable for bullets because you have to cold hammer the bullet into shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iteration X will find a way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:52:45-08:00","id":1042091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042072#post1042072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cold Iron while not clearly defined, is definitely barely processed, any bullet made for Modern gun wouldn't fit, you'd have to have a really old gun to have it work (with a risk of it exploding in your hands)<br /> And any magical attempt to create cold iron would fail, because that's what cold iron is.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that Changeling wipe the floor with Mage &amp; Technocrats, but they can definitely defend themselves.<br /> <br /> (and anyway most of this might change greatly with C20)</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that cold iron is crap for bullets there is no reason that magic can't create or teleport it. It's a material that happens to be banal, not condensed banality. <br /> <br /> Also magnetic acceleration would still work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:54:09-08:00","id":1042093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042084#post1042084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Iteration X will find a way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that's highly unlikely since the Union rarely actually pays attention to the 'traditional' means of fighting supernatural creatures. You don't see technocrats with chainguns that fire wooden stakes do you?<br /> <br /> The idea that they'd even think to use cold iron is kind of silly.<br /> <br /> It's actually one of their greatest downsides, compared to the traditions in crossover matches. The Union takes everything head on and ignores their splat based weaknesses for the most part. Unlike say the Hermetics, who have a spell that summons true sunlight to take on vampires with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T16:03:48-08:00","id":1042097,"title":"","content":"To be fair they used sunlight on Ravnos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T16:11:31-08:00","id":1042101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042091#post1042091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I agree that cold iron is crap for bullets there is no reason that magic can't create or teleport it. It's a material that happens to be banal, not condensed banality.<br /> <br /> Also magnetic acceleration would still work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Teleportation or Magnetic acceleration =&gt; countermagic, it has to be a mundane way (in this specific example)<br /> <br /> The material is banal by it's nature/essence, not by it's composition. creating it with magic will not create cold Iron in the Changeling sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T16:34:23-08:00","id":1042110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042101#post1042101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teleportation or Magnetic acceleration =&gt; countermagic, it has to be a mundane way (in this specific example)<br /> <br /> The material is banal by it's nature/essence, not by it's composition. creating it with magic will not create cold Iron in the Changeling sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems a strange loophole that even moving the stuff by magic takes its banality away.<br /> <br /> Edit: no wait, I see what you are saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T18:54:43-08:00","id":1042165,"title":"","content":"If putting Cold Iron into a bullet and firing it from a gun is too great an engineering challenge for Iteration X - a huge assumption - they could always go from the next best thing: cold iron-tipped crossbow bolts. It's not like such a technology has been lost over the ages; the Order of Reason was using them way back in the Sorcerer's Crusade. Crossbows, that is, not necessarily cold iron bolts. (Although, given that the Fey were considered credible threats by even &quot;rationalists&quot; at the time, they could very well have employed cold iron weapons during that era). You could also use air-pressure dart guns, with darts made or tipped in cold iron.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for making Cold Iron weapons, it comes down to whether the definition is &quot;has only been worked by hand hammering&quot;, or &quot;has never been heated&quot;. If it's the latter case, Iteration X has a potent answer to shaping metals without heat: pneumatic presses. They can beat raw ore into shape through mechanical strength.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for if the Union would ever try using Cold Iron, remember that part of the Technocracy's MO is finding ways to rationalize to themselves why such-and-such seemingly supernatural phenomenon can work under scientific principles. Obviously, the so-called &quot;Fairies&quot; are disrupted by the specific harmonic and chemical signature of iron ore, a property that is lost in purer forms of the metal or alloys.<br /> <br /> It's bullshit reasoning, but like hell a Technocrat is going to eschew that explanation in favor of &quot;because magic&quot;. They're scientists, dammit, and scientists are willing to go along with facts if the data supports them. Theories can come later, when they've had a chance to dissect the specimens post-mortem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T20:11:46-08:00","id":1042197,"title":"","content":"Wrought iron is impure iron, it has more carbon than steel but less than cast iron. Changeling could nap on a pure iron bench all day and feel nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T07:51:17-08:00","id":1042413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042093#post1042093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, that's highly unlikely since the Union rarely actually pays attention to the 'traditional' means of fighting supernatural creatures. You don't see technocrats with chainguns that fire wooden stakes do you?<br /> <br /> The idea that they'd even think to use cold iron is kind of silly.<br /> <br /> It's actually one of their greatest downsides, compared to the traditions in crossover matches. The Union takes everything head on and ignores their splat based weaknesses for the most part. Unlike say the Hermetics, who have a spell that summons true sunlight to take on vampires with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's almost as if the premise of &quot;technology is just another form of magic&quot; has a fatal breakdown state when it touches other games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T07:58:23-08:00","id":1042416,"title":"","content":"It really, really does. If technology is a form of True Magick, how could Changelings, Fera, Kindred, Wraiths, etc use it? That is why I think Hyperscience is True Magick with a funny hat rather than real science or real technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T08:54:13-08:00","id":1042451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042416#post1042416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really, really does. If technology is a form of True Magick, how could Changelings, Fera, Kindred, Wraiths, etc use it? That is why I think Hyperscience is True Magick with a funny hat rather than real science or real technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that each gameline runs on different &quot;fuel&quot; for magic.<br /> <br /> I don't know much about Vampire Disciplines, so I can't speak for it.<br /> But the Garou's powers come from spiritual empowerment, from the Umbra, from Gaia, and from the trinity. In many ways, the werewolf perspective is that Science is simply what humans interpret as the work of the Weaver, they do not question why things are consistent, they just accept they will be and leave it at that. Though any philosopher that has stated &quot;God keeps the world consistent&quot; is basically acknowledging the work of the Weaver.<br /> When Garou do magic, they call upon spiritual entities that have given them favour.<br /> Mages do the same, but the main difference is the method. Mages draw power from the avatar (or vice versa) in order to WANT things into being. The Garou use the relationship they have with the spirit world to FEEL them into being, be it through rage, piety, promises, or simply hope.<br /> Yes, there are many Mages who would say they use Emotion of Feelings as their focus, but the difference is that they still need to believe it works, they still need their will to guide it. Garou do not, they just Feel it. They are their powers.<br /> <br /> The arcanoi of Wraith are also emotion based, but it's not the same as the Garou's empowered stance. The Wraith's powers are more about trying to hold on, about desperately clinging to what you have so you don't lose it or get lost yourself. Their powers are about trying to reclaim control of that which they have lost, stay focused and not lose their way in the twisting worlds of the Underworld. While the Mages's powers are fuelled by a form of drive and determination, and the Garous by a need to fight on for that which they need, the Wraiths are fuelled by loss, or rather, by a desire to reclaim what was once lost.<br /> The Wraith acts not to empower itself like the other two, but because they refuse to be without.<br /> <br /> So Mage's powers are forces of embodied Will, Garou's are forces of Nature's Empowerd Emotions, and Wraith's are the pure Need to Remain Alive.<br /> <br /> The Changeling, on the other hand, have their magic from the emotion of whimsy, theirs is a life built on the old world dreams, when anything and everything was possible. Banality harms them so because taking things are part and understanding their limitations goes against this prospect. Theirs is the magic which exists in the &quot;could be&quot; and the &quot;try not to think about it too hard&quot; school of thought.<br /> The fuzzier the logic, and the greater the potential, the more power they are able to use. Theirs is the world of mystery and enchantment.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Mage Wants<br /> The Garou Must<br /> The Wraith Needs<br /> And the Fae Can","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T09:07:58-08:00","id":1042462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042413#post1042413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's almost as if the premise of &quot;technology is just another form of magic&quot; has a fatal breakdown state when it touches other games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's only another form of magic until it is accepted by the Consensus*. Even in Mage, once that happens it isn't affected by countermagic.<br /> <br /> *You can also say everything is Magic, but the accepted stuff is protected. The results are the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T10:16:13-08:00","id":1042497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042413#post1042413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's almost as if the premise of &amp;quot;technology is just another form of magic&amp;quot; has a fatal breakdown state when it touches other games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea the leaps of logic needed to conclude that was my point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T10:37:29-08:00","id":1042507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042497#post1042497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no idea the leaps of logic needed to conclude that was my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't commenting on the point of your post. Gushing bitterness over creative direction cited again, with an organization trying super-hard to change every game into a different genre, now, that's where it's at!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But the Garou's powers come from spiritual empowerment, from the Umbra, from Gaia, and from the trinity. In many ways, the werewolf perspective is that Science is simply what humans interpret as the work of the Weaver</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> No, the Book of the Weaver talks about the laws of physical existence being things that even the Weaver, amazingly enough, doesn't actually know in their entirety. The Weaver's role is to fix things and set them in a place with a definite form, not to create them. Try as it might, it just can't manage anything but splitting spirit and flesh away from each other.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T12:00:59-08:00","id":1042542,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Weaver does not usually create, that is the job of the Wyld, the Weaver maintains and shapes what is already created. If anything, the Wyld would be the creator of the laws of Reality, with the Weaver selectively reinforcing the laws of Reality that furthers Her plans (such as the separation of the Flesh from the Spirit, the Flesh from the Dream, and the Dream from the Spirit). Strangely enough, Science is an Incarna of the Weaver that suffers from horrible neglect because the Weaver does not want to encourage exploration and wonder and would probably abandon the Weaver for Gaia given sufficient incentive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T12:04:44-08:00","id":1042544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042451#post1042451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mage Wants<br /> The Garou Must<br /> The Wraith Needs<br /> And the Fae Can</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhhhh I love it (most of the reasoning behind too!)<br /> <br /> Maybe The Vampire Hunger? (or another synonym maybe?)<br /> <br /> Also on the whole Technology/Magic, I gues you can differentiate Magic(k) mimicking as Technology if a mundane (or other splat using mundane mean) is unable to reproduct the device.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T12:09:00-08:00","id":1042547,"title":"","content":"Or you could just say that Hyperscience is just a fancy name for True Magick that disguises itself as science and technology while science and technology are based on the laws of Fundamental Reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T12:26:01-08:00","id":1042552,"title":"","content":"Taking things back into the realm of science fiction in Changeling versus science fiction in Mage.<br /> <br /> Rick Sanchez. Etherite or Nocker?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T12:47:11-08:00","id":1042557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042547#post1042547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could just say that Hyperscience is just a fancy name for True Magick that disguises itself as science and technology while science and technology are based on the laws of Fundamental Reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that is that there are canonical examples of technocrat devices on the cusp of entering the consensus as standard technology. The thunderhead for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T13:40:48-08:00","id":1042576,"title":"","content":"Or it could be that the Union created the item through Hyperscience until they could learn to create it through conventional methods. I think that Rick Sanchez would be an Etherite who drags his acolyte grandson through the Deep Umbra in support of his research.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T13:52:42-08:00","id":1042584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042552#post1042552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking things back into the realm of science fiction in Changeling versus science fiction in Mage.<br /> <br /> Rick Sanchez. Etherite or Nocker?</div> </div> </div> </div>From Rick &amp; Morty?<br /> <br /> Etherite, all the way. Aside from the fact that his inventions are far greater in power than most Changlings, he just fits the theme of Hubris to a 'T'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T14:05:04-08:00","id":1042594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042547#post1042547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could just say that Hyperscience is just a fancy name for True Magick that disguises itself as science and technology while science and technology are based on the laws of Fundamental Reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Science&quot; is what the Consensus say it is; meaning, science is what the Technocracy say it is (with the eventual etherite or VA pollution on it).<br /> <br /> Airplanes can only fly because the technocrats set their time tables to allow it.<br /> <br /> What other splats do with technology is:<br /> A) Using their static powers on it to make them work beyond the initial parameters set by Consensus;<br /> B) Operate this technologies within the parameters of the Consensus.<br /> <br /> You can say anything you like about &quot;Fundamental Laws&quot;, and they may well exist, but it's <b><u><i>NOT SCIENCE </i></u></b>, simply because science is CONSENSUS.<br /> <br /> Do you doubt? Tell me exactly what kind of &quot;science&quot; says that a bird spirit can make an object or a person fly?<br /> <br /> &quot;Science&quot; does NOT account for magic.... And spirits... And beings of fairytales. Are the insane scene transmutations inside the Dreaming &quot;scientific&quot; at all?<br /> <br /> Take your super advanced machine made by your Brujah engeneer to the Dreaming and see just how well they will work, no matter how &quot;solidy&quot; were the &quot;scientific pr\u00ednciples&quot; that he applyed to make it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T14:31:07-08:00","id":1042607,"title":"","content":"About Changellings vs Mages:<br /> <br /> Mind 1 can protect Mages against the Mists. Just read the description of Mind 1.<br /> <br /> Mind 2 could generate glamour OR banality, creating a kind of &quot;creativity aura&quot; or &quot;dull aura&quot;. Most Mages don't know much of faeries to know that, they would probably do such things by accident, as an indirect action learnt true attempt-and-mistake (so, I've made an aura of dullness around me; those *faeries* or whatever they were runned away, cursing me). This would be an indetect effect; a Mage with profound knowledge of the kithain and the Dreaming however, could created glamour or banality <i>directly</i>, meaning that each success on Arete would create one temporary banality or glamour. The necessary spheres for that can be debatable - one could say you only need Mind 2; others could argue that Glamour and Banality are not just psychic emanations, but they are psychic emanations turned into a form of Ether; in that case, the Mage would need Mind 2 to generate the psychic emanations, Prime 4 to turn them into the &quot;quintessence&quot; (by this view, Changellings and chimeras are a sort of periapts that transform psychic emanations into quintessence - and banality and glamour would BOTH be quintessence, of diametral opposed ressonance). Others can say that Prime 2 is enough to generate the right ressonance to be &quot;condensated&quot; into banality or glamour, so you only need Prime 4 to generate Glamour or Banality. Mind 2 can still alter the banality/glamour of an area.<br /> <br /> Mind 3 can be used to &quot;enchant&quot; anyone, both the Mage himself and others. Oh yes, and Mind 1 can already perceive chimeras around.<br /> <br /> With Spirit 1, you can see the creature of the Dreaming and the fae mien of changellings.<br /> <br /> Mind 3 can create chimeras; with Prime 2, you can turn them permanent.<br /> <br /> With Mind 3, you can enter the Near Dreaming in Astral projection, tough that will be extremely dangerous if you don't know exactly what you're doing<br /> <br /> With Spirit 3, you can enter the Near Dreaming in physical form.<br /> <br /> With Spirit 4, you can &quot;Call the Wyrd&quot; yourself.<br /> <br /> For any of that, all you need is the <i>knowledge</i> of the Dreaming. For example: just turning your spiritual senses with spirit 1, will make you see the Penumbra. You need to know what you're looking for to be able to &quot;see fairies&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T14:43:22-08:00","id":1042613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042557#post1042557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with that is that there are canonical examples of technocrat devices on the cusp of entering the consensus as standard technology. The thunderhead for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also references to mundane technology that stops working in the isolated areas of the world. Although depending on how significant* baseline reality is some things may be completely mundane. So it could very well be a mix of both.<br /> <br /> *Edit: Poor word choice. I meant how many things are a part of baseline reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 02-02-2017, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T14:58:14-08:00","id":1042618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042557#post1042557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with that is that there are canonical examples of technocrat devices on the cusp of entering the consensus as standard technology. The thunderhead for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's putting it mildly. I remember the 'DCMD's from the Technomancer's Toybox. Tiny little cameras that transfer their signal wirelessy, while being disguised as trash and small items.<br /> <br /> ...yeah. That was a magickal Technocracy hypertech item in that 1998 book (And thus also roughly the 1998 in-game time).<br /> Guess what you can make easily yourself these days? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Every smartphone we hold in our hands these days would have been Hypertech back then. A supercomputer that fits into your palm, with a touch display, network connectivity and graphics that no machine back then could remotely reach. In. Your. Palm. Like, it feeds off a small battery. Absolute Hypertech material in that age. Now every sleeper's running around with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 02-02-2017, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T15:05:52-08:00","id":1042621,"title":"","content":"No, that is not how the Mists and the Dreaming works in cWoD. Mage (Revised) was written after Changeling (2e), so if the writers had intended for Mages to be able to defeat the Mists, then they would have put it in the Mage books (just like they did with the rules concerning Delirium and the Fog). There is nothing, as it is written in Changeling or Mage, that Mages can do to defeat the Mists or to defy the Dreaming, so any attempts to avoid the rules as written is just headcanon.<br /> <br /> Now, Mages can perceive Chimera, the Kinain, the Kithain and the Near Dreaming with Spirit because the Dreaming is a spiritual universe, not a mental universe, but their ability to remember what they perceive is based on their Banality. Technomancers are incapable, because of their Banality, to remember anything about the Dreaming or the denizens of the Dreaming, beyond fragments of memory. Their technology fails and their magic fails because the Dreaming is greater than any Mage. Of course, STs can change any rules that they want in their games, but the canon rules are the canon rules, and no amount of argument is going to change what the writer wrote. In addition, I think that it is wonderful that there is something that is immune to the hubris of Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T15:06:22-08:00","id":1042622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042607#post1042607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 1 can protect Mages against the Mists. Just read the description of Mind 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd need a reason to shield yourself though and as soon as you drop the protection your memories will fade<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042607#post1042607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 2 could generate glamour OR banality, creating a kind of &quot;creativity aura&quot; or &quot;dull aura&quot;. Most Mages don't know much of faeries to know that, they would probably do such things by accident, as an indirect action learnt true attempt-and-mistake (so, I've made an aura of dullness around me; those *faeries* or whatever they were runned away, cursing me).</div> </div> </div> </div>Dullness/Creativity is not the same as Banality/Glamour.<br /> Mind 2 should not be enough it's like saying to create Vampire Vitae you'd need the same level of life than to create normal blood, with no other Sphere<br /> ...Why would a mage create an aura of dullness?<br /> Changeling wouldn't flee away cursing a sudden raise in banality, they might get away but doing their best to not be detected it could be Autumn People/Fae<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042607#post1042607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be an indetect effect; a Mage with profound knowledge of the kithain and the Dreaming however, could created glamour or banality <i>directly</i>, meaning that each success on Arete would create one temporary banality or glamour. The necessary spheres for that can be debatable - one could say you only need Mind 2; others could argue that Glamour and Banality are not just psychic emanations, but they are psychic emanations turned into a form of Ether; in that case, the Mage would need Mind 2 to generate the psychic emanations, Prime 4 to turn them into the &quot;quintessence&quot; (by this view, Changellings and chimeras are a sort of periapts that transform psychic emanations into quintessence - and banality and glamour would BOTH be quintessence, of diametral opposed ressonance). Others can say that Prime 2 is enough to generate the right ressonance to be &quot;condensated&quot; into banality or glamour, so you only need Prime 4 to generate Glamour or Banality. Mind 2 can still alter the banality/glamour of an area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing that the rules more or less equate Caerns/Freeholds/Nodes, it should be equivalently hard to produce by Mages, though the Sphere to use would vary<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042607#post1042607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 3 can be used to &quot;enchant&quot; anyone, both the Mage himself and others. Oh yes, and Mind 1 can already perceive chimeras around.<br /> <br /> With Spirit 1, you can see the creature of the Dreaming and the fae mien of changellings.<br /> <br /> Mind 3 can create chimeras; with Prime 2, you can turn them permanent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm quite sure it's more Spirit, you're interpreting the Chimera &amp; dreaming as psychic creatures born for the Dream, while they are more creature from the essence of the Dreaming taking shape by people special link with said Dreaming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042607#post1042607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Mind 3, you can enter the Near Dreaming in Astral projection, tough that will be extremely dangerous if you don't know exactly what you're doing<br /> <br /> With Spirit 3, you can enter the Near Dreaming in physical form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah entering the Dreaming is not a good idea for Mages, though the Near Dreaming isn't that bad, just don't go further...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042607#post1042607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Spirit 4, you can &quot;Call the Wyrd&quot; yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>What?<br /> Why?<br /> Calling the Wyrd, is the Fae taking is fae mien in the Mundane world &amp; having is Arts having physical effects rather than Chimerical... what's the point for a Mage???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T15:07:27-08:00","id":1042623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042584#post1042584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From Rick &amp; Morty?<br /> <br /> Etherite, all the way. Aside from the fact that his inventions are far greater in power than most Changlings, he just fits the theme of Hubris to a 'T'.</div> </div> </div> </div>See I was actually leaning more Nocker. He's got the profanity, the existential despair, and the portals to a dizzying array of places seemingly limited solely by one's ability to conceive them aren't difficult to sell as Trods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T15:44:26-08:00","id":1042642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042621#post1042621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that is not how the Mists and the Dreaming works in cWoD. Mage (Revised) was written after Changeling (2e), so if the writers had intended for Mages to be able to defeat the Mists, then they would have put it in the Mage books (just like they did with the rules concerning Delirium and the Fog). There is nothing, as it is written in Changeling or Mage, that Mages can do to defeat the Mists or to defy the Dreaming, so any attempts to avoid the rules as written is just headcanon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate saying this, but I always got the impression that the other lines didn't pay much attention to Changeling. I'd interpret the omission as an oversight. Especially since Revised was so busy dealing with all of the massive changes to Mage itself.<br /> <br /> Also, it kind of conflicts with the themes of Mage to have Mages mostly unable to interact with something, so in this case Changeling's input has to be taken with a grain of salt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T15:57:57-08:00","id":1042651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042623#post1042623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See I was actually leaning more Nocker. He's got the profanity, the existential despair, and the portals to a dizzying array of places seemingly limited solely by one's ability to conceive them aren't difficult to sell as Trods.</div> </div> </div> </div>But an Etherite can also be burdened with existential despair (M20 has an entire Paradigm for it - &quot;One Way Trip To Oblivion&quot;). And an Etherite has access to the Umbra, which is also a realm of potentially limitless places. If anything, he has MORE places to go if he has the entire Umbra to explore, and not just the Dreaming (since, of course, the Dreaming is one part of the Umbra). And Mages are certainly not deprived of their ability to swear. Profanity could easily be taken as an Instrument for Magick/Science unto itself. As can alcohol, a vice Rick imbibes heavily.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm not saying Rick couldn't be run as a Nocker. All I AM saying is that every aspect of his character that could make him a Nocker could also make him an Etherite of the &quot;Mad Scientist&quot; faction, and more easily. He also wouldn't be shackled to the ethos of fairy beings, like looking for trods to access the Dreaming or harvesting Glamour from creative people. He could build a flying car for his Stepping Sideways needs, and harvest Quintessence using scientific instruments or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 02-02-2017, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T16:33:37-08:00","id":1042667,"title":"","content":"But Changeling paid attention to the other lines, which is why it names specific Arcanoi, Disciplibes, Gifts, Spheres, etc. In many ways, Changeling was designed to be the most crossover friendly cWoD gamelan because many of its authors worked on the other game lines as well (Mark Rein was one of the original creators of Changeling and Mage).<br /> <br /> The Dreaming is a separate Universe from the Umbra (the Dream Zone is different than the Dreaming). The Dreaming is a separate infinity from the Umbra, though the Paths of Balor connect the Dreaming to the Umbra. The reason why Etherite makes more sense than Nickerson though is Ricky is too banal to be a Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T17:17:12-08:00","id":1042689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042667#post1042667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Changeling paid attention to the other lines, which is why it names specific Arcanoi, Disciplibes, Gifts, Spheres, etc. In many ways, Changeling was designed to be the most crossover friendly cWoD gamelan because many of its authors worked on the other game lines as well (Mark Rein was one of the original creators of Changeling and Mage).<br /> <br /> The Dreaming is a separate Universe from the Umbra (the Dream Zone is different than the Dreaming). The Dreaming is a separate infinity from the Umbra, though the Paths of Balor connect the Dreaming to the Umbra. The reason why Etherite makes more sense than Nickerson though is Ricky is too banal to be a Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling is also a specific line with specific powers that do specific explicit things.<br /> <br /> Mage is not. Mage has powers that do broad vague things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T17:39:11-08:00","id":1042703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042651#post1042651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But an Etherite can also be burdened with existential despair (M20 has an entire Paradigm for it - &quot;One Way Trip To Oblivion&quot;). And an Etherite has access to the Umbra, which is also a realm of potentially limitless places. If anything, he has MORE places to go if he has the entire Umbra to explore, and not just the Dreaming (since, of course, the Dreaming is one part of the Umbra). And Mages are certainly not deprived of their ability to swear. Profanity could easily be taken as an Instrument for Magick/Science unto itself. As can alcohol, a vice Rick imbibes heavily.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm not saying Rick couldn't be run as a Nocker. All I AM saying is that every aspect of his character that could make him a Nocker could also make him an Etherite of the &quot;Mad Scientist&quot; faction, and more easily. He also wouldn't be shackled to the ethos of fairy beings, like looking for trods to access the Dreaming or harvesting Glamour from creative people. He could build a flying car for his Stepping Sideways needs, and harvest Quintessence using scientific instruments or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I am likewise not saying he couldn't be an Etherite. My point was that profanity is a specific feature of the Nocker kith, and existential despair is a fairly common refrain for Changelings in particular. My argument for the Dreaming as many-universes depends a bit on how you think about the metaphysics of both the show and the gameline. My contention here (for the sake of this thought experiment only) would be that since R&amp;M seems to be operating on the theory of infinite universes of infinite possibility, based on so many alternative might-have-beens that if one can imagine a particular reality the odds of it existing rapidly approach one, that the Dreaming as a physical representation of the collective unconscious has the potential to contain and accommodate any such reality. Given the particular whimsical nature of many of these universes, it seems to fit in Changeling's general wheelhouse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T18:35:05-08:00","id":1042729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042622#post1042622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd need a reason to shield yourself though and as soon as you drop the protection your memories will fade</div> </div> </div> </div>True, however, there is no reason to NOT have a shield always on. On the other hand, if the Mage drops the shield for whatever reason, he can always recover ALL his memories using Mind 1.<br /> <br /> A Mage can also use Mind 1 to always keep his Willpower at 10, if he can keep with the pattern leaking. Will 10 will make he total immune to the mists.<br /> <br /> He can also &quot;store&quot; his memories (in a computer? In a mirror?) for &quot;later use&quot;<br /> <br /> Or, just make a talisman using Prime 4 to place a Mind 1 effect to always protect him from the Mists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042622#post1042622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dullness/Creativity is not the same as Banality/Glamour.<br /> Mind 2 should not be enough it's like saying to create Vampire Vitae you'd need the same level of life than to create normal blood, with no other Sphere</div> </div> </div> </div>It turns the blood into Vampiric Vitae if the Vampire drinks it, isn't it?<br /> <br /> It's the same principle with a dulness/creativity aura (both can be done with Mind 2). Without changellings around (or chimeras), it's just a borderline schizofreniac impulse for creativity and imagination, or a strong felling of hopeless boredom. But, if a changelling is close, it will &quot;destilate&quot; those emocional emanations into glamour or Banality.<br /> <br /> Tell me, does the dreamers have glamour of them own?<br /> <br /> So, how can the changellings &quot;extract&quot; glamour out of them? Or, be infected by their banality?<br /> <br /> It's just THE SAME principle for a wraith: a Mage can use Mind 2 to artificially generate an emotion; if it is related to one of the wraiths passions (or dark passions), the wraith can &quot;destilate&quot; that emotion into pathos (or Angst).<br /> <br /> The Mage himself is not generating Pathos or Angst (unless he uses Prime and have a good amount of knowledge about wraiths), he is just allowing the wraiths to &quot;filter&quot; the emanations.<br /> <br /> Ok, imagine it like this: we can't synthesize sugar using only CO2 and H2O. But, if we turn a light on, we can use a plant to make it for us.<br /> <br /> When a mage make a creativity/dulness &quot;aura&quot;, or when emanating emotions like Love, Piety etc that can be the core passions of a wraith, or when creating an aura of Hate, Lust etc, that can be a dark passion of a wraith, he is NOT creating glamour/banality or pathos/angst. He is turning a light on, that will allow changellings or wraiths to generate them.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, that means that, for a Changelling or a Wraith, having a Mage with Mind 2 as a friend is fucking awesome... And an easy source for infinity &quot;juice&quot;. That's, at least, RAW.<br /> <br /> For a Mage, Mind 2 is a great way to have wraiths and changellings as allies... Also, your Mage can keep the ally always well fed and well empowered to better help... That's an incredible sinergy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042622#post1042622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Why would a mage create an aura of dullness?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing that I said: the Mage must know EXACTLY what's he's doing. That implies a good amounts of knowledge about the fae. A Mage with no knowledge of changellings would have no idea of how to deal with one - well... More or less... The Mage could use Entropy 1 to figure it out the weaknesses of changellings... With enough successes, he could see that those &quot;strange lunatics with strange etherial emanations&quot; have a problem with bore people and with Cold Iron...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042622#post1042622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling wouldn't flee away cursing a sudden raise in banality, they might get away but doing their best to not be detected it could be Autumn People/Fae</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to be so literal. It were just a dramatization of an hypotetical situation<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042622#post1042622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing that the rules more or less equate Caerns/Freeholds/Nodes, it should be equivalently hard to produce by Mages, though the Sphere to use would vary</div> </div> </div> </div>For Mages, all those are Nodes, with radically different ressonances. Yes, using Prime to generate Glamour or Banality <i>directly</i> (which means, quintessence with the <i>right</i> ressonance) could be hard indeed, as much as &quot;filtering&quot; quintessence into Gnosis or Pathos; maybe you'd need Prime 3/Spirit 2 to create Gnosis, Prime 3/Mind 2 (and/or Spirit 2) to create Pathos/Angst or Glamour/Banality. For ANY of those, the Mage will require <i>espec\u00edfic</i> knowledge about the subject (althouth, using Prime 1 to see the &quot;energies&quot; of those beings should be enough at least to try, but perhaps, without further research on the topic, it would be made with a +3 dif for doing the effect without proper foci, which would make the feat very hard for a Mage that never studied those ressonances).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042622#post1042622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quite sure it's more Spirit, you're interpreting the Chimera &amp; dreaming as psychic creatures born for the Dream, while they are more creature from the essence of the Dreaming taking shape by people special link with said Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Create chimeras is done with Mind 3, which allies you to create ilusions. Just like the vampiric discipline Chimeirism, those ilusions are Chimeras. With Prime 2 and a point of Quintessence, you can give them substance to persist in the Dreaming (once again, you'd have to know that the ilusions you create, generate chimeras; if you don't know nothing about chimeras or the Dreaming, how would you know that you can make them with Mind 3/Prime 2?)<br /> <br /> That effect (create chimeras - Mind 3/Prime 2, 1 Quint point) can be a powerful tool for those that study the Dreaming (specially if you know what you're doing, and use it to create powerful chimerical alllies).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042622#post1042622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah entering the Dreaming is not a good idea for Mages, though the Near Dreaming isn't that bad, just don't go further...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042622#post1042622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What?<br /> Why?<br /> Calling the Wyrd, is the Fae taking is fae mien in the Mundane world &amp; having is Arts having physical effects rather than Chimerical... what's the point for a Mage???</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, let me explain: when I said that Mages can call the Wyrd, I did use &quot; &quot;.<br /> <br /> Actually, with Spirit 4, you tear apart the barriers of the worlds. You can use it to tear the Gauntlet, allowing spirits to enter the material world, or tearing the shroud to allow ghosts. In both cases, when you do that, spirits and ghosts materialize.<br /> <br /> So... If you do the same, but with the Dreaming... Well, the effect is the same as &quot;calling the Wyrd&quot; (but it's a lot harder for Mages to do it, mind you).<br /> <br /> And why would a Mage do that?<br /> <br /> Well, if he spent a good amount of time using Mind 3/Prime 2 to create several chimerical friends and chimerical weapons and exosqueletons machines, it is not a bad idea turning all those &quot;ilusions&quot; real to give a helpful hand...<br /> <br /> By the way, Mind 3/Prime 2 can CREATE chimeras, but to CHANGE them (or others he haven't created himself), the Mage will need Spirit 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T18:43:27-08:00","id":1042731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042703#post1042703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, I am likewise not saying he couldn't be an Etherite. My point was that profanity is a specific feature of the Nocker kith, and existential despair is a fairly common refrain for Changelings in particular. My argument for the Dreaming as many-universes depends a bit on how you think about the metaphysics of both the show and the gameline. My contention here (for the sake of this thought experiment only) would be that since R&amp;M seems to be operating on the theory of infinite universes of infinite possibility, based on so many alternative might-have-beens that if one can imagine a particular reality the odds of it existing rapidly approach one, that the Dreaming as a physical representation of the collective unconscious has the potential to contain and accommodate any such reality. Given the particular whimsical nature of many of these universes, it seems to fit in Changeling's general wheelhouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, the High Umbra also have that aspect of &quot;limitless possibilities&quot;.<br /> <br /> I have always seen the Dreaming and the High Umbra individualization as an artificial one rather than something that really makes sense, but it is Cannon, they are different places, and as it is written, the High Umbra would be the universe of <i>thoughts</i>, and the Dreaming the universe of <i>imagination</i>... But honestly, it's a definition too fickle, it would be best to make them both to be the same place","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T19:02:06-08:00","id":1042740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042621#post1042621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that is not how the Mists and the Dreaming works in cWoD. Mage (Revised) was written after Changeling (2e), so if the writers had intended for Mages to be able to defeat the Mists, then they would have put it in the Mage books (just like they did with the rules concerning Delirium and the Fog). There is nothing, as it is written in Changeling or Mage, that Mages can do to defeat the Mists or to defy the Dreaming, so any attempts to avoid the rules as written is just headcanon.<br /> <br /> Now, Mages can perceive Chimera, the Kinain, the Kithain and the Near Dreaming with Spirit because the Dreaming is a spiritual universe, not a mental universe, but their ability to remember what they perceive is based on their Banality. Technomancers are incapable, because of their Banality, to remember anything about the Dreaming or the denizens of the Dreaming, beyond fragments of memory. Their technology fails and their magic fails because the Dreaming is greater than any Mage. Of course, STs can change any rules that they want in their games, but the canon rules are the canon rules, and no amount of argument is going to change what the writer wrote. In addition, I think that it is wonderful that there is something that is immune to the hubris of Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's like saying &quot;The Underworld is greater than any Mage&quot;., and because of it, it is impossible for the living to travel there.<br /> <br /> Thats however, is absolutely untrue.<br /> <br /> Mages are supposed to be able to do ANYTHING. That's the thing about TRUE magik.<br /> <br /> The world &quot;impossible&quot; is anathema for Mages.<br /> <br /> For a Mage, &quot;impossible&quot; is a challenge to go further.<br /> <br /> Thats the motto of the game. You're only limited by yourself.<br /> <br /> About perceiving the Dreaming, Mages can walk on dreams with Mind 3.<br /> <br /> The High Umbra is also a spiritual world, but you can reach it with Mind 4. So, it has no ground to say its only Spirit. <br /> <br /> Also, don't forget that chimeras are created by the imagination. Chimeras roaming around in the material world could be detected with Mind 1 (not seeing, just perceived). I also consider that to be true for spirits and ghosts (they do have minds after all). And spirit 1 can see them. <br /> <br /> To attack Chimera, spirit 2, or Prime<br /> <br /> To create chimeras, Mind 3 or Spirit 5<br /> <br /> To explore the Dreaming, Mind 3 (Astral form) or Spirit 3 (physical form).<br /> <br /> Banality, Glamour, Mind 2 (indirect) or Prime 4 (direct)<br /> <br /> &quot;Enchanting&quot; self or other, Mind 3<br /> <br /> Change Chimera, Spirit 4<br /> <br /> &quot;Calling the Wyrd&quot; Spirit 4<br /> <br /> Protection from the Mists, Mind 1.<br /> <br /> Detect Chimeras Mind 1, or see the chimericals Spirit 1<br /> <br /> Those are some examples of how to deal with the Dreaming... If one knows what they are doing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: now that I came to think of, creating Glamour or Banality, it wouldn't be Prime 4... You'd have to use Prime 4 AND Mind 2 to create glamour/banality &quot;out of thin air&quot; (meaning, you would generate the psychic emanations that are transformed in those types of energies by the creatures of the Dreaming, and immediatly &quot;destilating&quot; them into the juice). To transmutate some form of quintessence (the one the Mage has stored in his Avatar, or flowing freely in a Node for example) into Glamour OR Banality, he would need Prime 2 (to change the ressonance), but if the changelling can't take that Glamour (or banality) by himself, the Mage won't be able to give it (for example, if the Mage changes his quintessence storaged in his Avatar into Glamour, the changelling can take it... And what follows is that the Mage will have enchanted himself). To share quintessence with changellings in the form of glamour or banality, the Mage will need Prime 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-02-2017, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T19:06:37-08:00","id":1042743,"title":"","content":"As to using true magick to 'call the wyrd' it seems to me that it would be easier to use Enchant life/object to modify your ethereal form and gear. Then pull that form through the gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T19:54:22-08:00","id":1042765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042743#post1042743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to using true magick to 'call the wyrd' it seems to me that it would be easier to use Enchant life/object to modify your ethereal form and gear. Then pull that form through the gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, for a Mage, &quot;call the Wyrd&quot; would require an extensive ritual and lots of successes.<br /> <br /> It's important to note however, that most Mages won't have a clue about what they're dealing with. Even Mages who are Masters in all those 3 spheres most useful to deal with the Fae (Spirit, Mind, Prime), if he doesn't know ANYTHING about the Dreaming and it's denizens, he will be almost powerless against changellings. That is, unless he start studying them.<br /> <br /> The majority of Mages won't know ANY of those effects, and it will be VERY hard to develop them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T20:41:14-08:00","id":1042782,"title":"","content":"What Gauntlet? There is no Gauntlet between the Autumn World and the Dreaming. If you do not go in through the ways allowed by the rules of the Dreaming, you are not getting in. <br /> <br /> By the way, Mind has nothing to do with the Dreaming. The Spheres that affect the Near Dreaming are Spirit and Prime, it says so specifically in the crossover rules for Mages in the Book of Lost Dreams. The Dreaming is not part of the Umbra, it is literally the otherside of the coin from the Umbra. If you do not believe me, please read the rules yourself, the books are available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-02-2017, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T21:04:58-08:00","id":1042788,"title":"","content":"Mind 1 is required alongside spirit 1 to view the near dreaming. It stands to reason that this continues as per normal advancement of sphere control.<br /> <br /> Book of worlds apparently is where that came from. Though I have not read it first hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T21:32:52-08:00","id":1042799,"title":"","content":"M20 also says Mind is required to do stuff with Changelings.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think it's kinda cool that each supernatural creature requires different spheres to interact with them.<br /> <br /> Matter and Life for Vampires<br /> Spirit and Life for Werewolves<br /> Spirit and Entropy for Wraiths (if you're foolish, otherwise Spirit works just as well)<br /> Prime and Spirit/Mind for Fae","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T03:30:22-08:00","id":1042874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042782#post1042782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Gauntlet? There is no Gauntlet between the Autumn World and the Dreaming. If you do not go in through the ways allowed by the rules of the Dreaming, you are not getting in. <br /> <br /> By the way, Mind has nothing to do with the Dreaming. The Spheres that affect the Near Dreaming are Spirit and Prime, it says so specifically in the crossover rules for Mages in the Book of Lost Dreams. The Dreaming is not part of the Umbra, it is literally the otherside of the coin from the Umbra. If you do not believe me, please read the rules yourself, the books are available.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, that's like saying &quot;The Underworld is not part of the Umbra&quot;.<br /> <br /> And I never said anything about a &quot;Gauntlet&quot; with the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> You seen to give too much of an importance to the Dream and changellings. Like it has been said, the other splats don't honor this game as it should; anyway, the book of worlds says you need Mind.. So, which source should I trust? The one SPECIFIC for Mages or the one of the other splat talking about them? If a Mage suplement say for example that changellings are allergic to technology... Should we believe it?<br /> <br /> Besides, just read the descriptions of the Mind Sphere. You'll see it has EVERYTHING to do with the Dreaming (Mind 3 allowing you to walk on dreams for instance, much like mind 4 allows you to enter the Astral Umbra)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T06:18:35-08:00","id":1042899,"title":"","content":"Of course, when we have more recent books with more detailed rules, it go with the more recent books with more detailed rules (the Book of Worlds was published in 1996 while the Book of Lost Dreams was published in 1997). Which do we believe? The book with rules that have been superceded by Changeling and Mage books (the Book of Lost Worlds was superceded by the Infinite Tapestry in Mage) and only had a paragraph on the Dreaming or the gameline with multiple books on the subject?<br /> <br /> Dreams are separate from the Dreaming. The Dreaming is built on the dreams after they have been dreamt, not while they are dreaming, so the Dreaming is built off of the spirits of dreams. By the time of Changeling (2e), the writers had separated to Dreaming from the Umbra, so much so that it is not even mentioned in the Infinite Tapestry as a place where Mages can go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T06:40:48-08:00","id":1042906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042899#post1042899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, when we have more recent books with more detailed rules, it go with the more recent books with more detailed rules (the Book of Worlds was published in 1996 while the Book of Lost Dreams was published in 1997). Which do we believe? The book with rules that have been superceded by Changeling and Mage books (the Book of Lost Worlds was superceded by the Infinite Tapestry in Mage) and only had a paragraph on the Dreaming or the gameline with multiple books on the subject?</div> </div> </div> </div>We go with Mage when we're playing Mage and Changeling when we are playing Changeling, and chose according to our needs with crossovers. Changeling rules are informative and they are worthy of consideration, but they do not have a casting vote over other game lines. <br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, there are already Mage books that we have to discard chunks of because they are at odds with the basic contents of the line. HDYDT is only the most recent example. We've invented entire terminologies to describe which of the contradictory explanations of the Magic rules we are using. If we can approach the Mage books themselves with that much skepticism and discernment, we can certainly apply the same attitude towards Changeling books.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T09:36:31-08:00","id":1043606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038176-is-mage-actually-more-appropriate-for-science-fiction-than-changeling?p=1042906#post1042906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We go with Mage when we're playing Mage and Changeling when we are playing Changeling, and chose according to our needs with crossovers. Changeling rules are informative and they are worthy of consideration, but they do not have a casting vote over other game lines. <br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, there are already Mage books that we have to discard chunks of because they are at odds with the basic contents of the line. HDYDT is only the most recent example. We've invented entire terminologies to describe which of the contradictory explanations of the Magic rules we are using. If we can approach the Mage books themselves with that much skepticism and discernment, we can certainly apply the same attitude towards Changeling books.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, we can read everything and pick and choose which pieces you like which could be fun things for your own game.<br /> <br /> If we can't be flexible about how the umbra works, what hope is there for the rest of the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}